        spec: "Stole property of {V}, a utility, valued at $900, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D} cut a charging cable off a station on {DATE}. The cut came at 2 a.m., and the utility's report came at 8 a.m. The charging station was in service at the time.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Station Camera", "{D} cuts the cable."), E(.document, 2, "Replacement Invoice", "$900 to replace the charging cable.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Scrap", "{DL} says it was broken scrap.")],
        role: "Utility technician",
        exam: [.direct("What did you find at the charging station on {DATE}?", "\"The charging cable had been cut off. The cut came at about 2 a.m., and my report came at 8.\""), .direct("What does the station camera show?", "\"It shows {D} cutting the cable. It shows the cut clearly.\""), .direct("What did it cost to replace?", "\"$900. The charging station was in service at the time, so the damage put it out of use.\""), .direct("Where is the charging station and how is it used?", "\"It sits in a public parking lot by a shopping center and serves four vehicles. Drivers plug in a cable, and the station draws power from a utility line.\""), .direct("What did you find at the scene?", "\"A cable cut cleanly at the base, with the copper cores exposed and the cut end missing. The station's display was dark and showed an error.\""), .direct("What was the cable worth?", "\"The replacement cost $900 with labor and a new connector. The station was out of service for two days while we ordered parts.\""), .cross("{DL} says it was broken scrap, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"The cable was working and in service, not scrap, at the time.\""), .cross("Did you see {DL} cut it?", "\"I saw it on the camera. I wasn't there at 2 a.m.\""), .cross("Was the cable damaged before?", "\"Not that I know of. I had no report of damage. It was in service.\""), .cross("The station was live when the cable was cut, wasn't it?", "\"Our records say the station was powered on, though no one was charging at 2 a.m. A live cable is dangerous to cut.\""), .cross("You do not know what {D} did with the cable afterward, do you?", "\"I do not. I only know the cut end was gone and the lot camera shows {DL} carrying a length of cable to a vehicle.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} cut a cable.", "Scrap."),
        allocution: "\"I found that cable lying near the station and thought it was broken scrap. It looked dead, and I didn't check. I'm truly sorry. I didn't realize it was connected, and I'd have left it if I had.\"",
        truths: ("The cable was in service.", "{DL} sold copper that day."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why did you cut the cable?", "\"I thought it was broken scrap. It was lying near the station, and I figured it was junk.\""), .direct("Did you know it was part of the station?", "\"No. It looked like a dead cable. I didn't check. I am truly sorry.\""), .direct("What did you do with it?", "\"I took it. I didn't realize it was connected. I'd have left it if I had known.\""), .direct("What were you doing in the lot at 2 a.m.?", "\"I was driving home from a late shift and saw a cable hanging from the station that looked abandoned. I pulled over to see.\""), .direct("What did you think the cable was?", "\"Scrap from a removed unit, because it hung loose and the screen was dark. I figured the owner had thrown it out.\""), .direct("What did you do with the copper?", "\"I sold it at a scrap yard later that day for about forty dollars. I did not hide what I was selling.\""), .cross("The camera shows you cutting it from the station, doesn't it?", "\"It shows me cutting a cable. I didn't realize it was live. I'm not an electrician.\""), .cross("It was 2 a.m., wasn't it?", "\"Yes. I was out late. I should have waited and looked in the daylight.\""), .cross("The station was in service, wasn't it?", "\"I've been told that. I didn't know. If I'd seen the lights, I'd have known.\""), .cross("You brought a cutter with you, didn't you?", "\"I keep cutters in my truck for work. I used them without thinking, and now I see it was the wrong place.\""), .cross("The cable was not lying on the ground, was it?", "\"No, it was attached to the station. I did not look closely.\"")],
        openings: ("At 2 a.m., a station camera shows {D} cutting a charging cable off an in-service station. The utility reported the damage at 8 a.m., and replacing the cable cost $900.", "The defense evidence includes someone who thought a cable was scrap, did not realize it was live, and sold the copper openly. {D} had no idea the cable belonged to a working station."),
        closings: ("A cable cut at 2 a.m. from a station in service, on camera, and a $900 bill. A cable attached to a station is not scrap, whatever the hour.", "{D} thought it was scrap and cut it openly in front of a camera. The State has not proved {DL} knew the cable was part of a working station."),
        timeline: [(0, "2 a.m.: the cut."), (0, "8 a.m.: the report.")],
        identified: "Station Camera",
        mood: .indifferent,
        genders: ["D": .male])

