        law: "disorderly",
        spec: "Disturbed the peace by violent conduct, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: false,
        summary: "{D} tore a ticket and screamed at a parking officer on {DATE}. The ticket was written at noon, and the scream came five minutes later. The meter had expired.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Street Camera", "{D} tears the ticket."), E(.statement, 2, "Parking Officer", "Heard {D} scream after the ticket was torn.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Upset", "{DL} says {D.he} was upset.")],
        role: "Parking officer",
        exam: [.direct("What happened on the street at noon?", "\"I wrote a ticket for an expired meter at noon. Five minutes later {D} tore it up and screamed at me.\""), .direct("What does the street camera show?", "\"It shows {DL} tearing the ticket in front of me and shouting. The video shows the tearing, and I heard the screaming.\""), .direct("Did you ask {D} to leave?", "\"Yes. I told {D.him} twice to leave the area. {D.He} kept shouting.\""), .direct("What was the parking situation on that block?", "\"It is a two-hour metered strip downtown with a lot of turnover. The meter at that space had run out about fifteen minutes before I wrote the citation.\""), .direct("What did you do when you wrote the ticket?", "\"I scanned the plate, wrote the violation, and tucked the ticket under the wiper. {D.He} walked up as I was finishing and asked me to cancel it.\""), .direct("What did the defendant do next?", "\"{D.He} took the ticket from the windshield, ripped it in half, and threw it on the ground. Then the screaming started, about a minute later.\""), .cross("The meter was expired, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. The meter was expired, and that is why I wrote the ticket.\""), .cross("Did the defendant threaten you?", "\"No. {D.He} screamed but did not threaten me or touch me.\""), .cross("How long did the screaming last?", "\"A few minutes, until {D.he} walked away.\""), .cross("{D} had some money in the meter at one point, didn't {D.he}?", "\"The meter showed a prior payment that had expired. {D.He} may have been inside a shop and lost track of time.\""), .cross("You did not call for backup, did you?", "\"No. I told {D.him} twice to leave the area, and {D.he} eventually walked away on {D.his} own.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} screamed at an officer.", "Upset."),
        allocution: "\"I'd been running late and got a ticket I thought was unfair, and I tore it up in front of the officer. I raised my voice and lost my temper. I'm sorry for how I acted toward someone just doing a job. I'll pay the fine.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} was told to leave twice.", "The meter was expired."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you tear the ticket?", "\"Yes, I did. I was upset about it, and I tore it up in front of the officer.\""), .direct("Did you scream?", "\"Yes. I raised my voice. I was frustrated and I lost my temper.\""), .direct("Why were you upset?", "\"I thought the ticket was unfair. I had been running late and got a ticket for only a few minutes.\""), .direct("Why had you parked there?", "\"I stopped for a ten-minute errand at the pharmacy, but the line was long. I came out and saw the officer writing.\""), .direct("What did you say to the officer?", "\"I said it had only been a few minutes over and asked for a break. The officer said the ticket was written and could not be undone.\""), .direct("What happened after you tore the ticket?", "\"I yelled that it was a money grab and that the city only cared about fines. I did not touch the officer, and I did not curse at anyone in particular.\""), .cross("You were told twice to leave, weren't you?", "\"Yes. I did not leave right away. I was still upset.\""), .cross("You tore up an official ticket, didn't you?", "\"I did. I know that was not right. I feel awful about it.\""), .cross("The meter had expired, hadn't it?", "\"It had. I read the display and saw zero, and I did not argue about that.\""), .cross("You argued with the officer for five minutes before you screamed, didn't you?", "\"Yes, I stood there for about five minutes arguing before I lost my temper completely and yelled.\""), .cross("The officer had already walked away when you started screaming, hadn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes, the officer was heading back to the cruiser. I yelled anyway, and I regret that. It was not the officer's fault the meter ran out.\"")],
        openings: ("A parking officer wrote a ticket for an expired meter at noon. Five minutes later, a street camera recorded {D} tearing the ticket and screaming at the officer, who twice asked {DL} to leave.", "Weigh the defense proof, which will show that {D} was upset over a ticket, raised a voice, and never touched or threatened the officer. {D.He} left on {D.his} own once the anger passed."),
        closings: ("An expired meter, a ticket torn up in front of the officer, and screaming after two requests to leave. The camera shows it, and the officer was only doing the job.", "A short outburst over a parking ticket, with no threat and no touching. Anger over a fine is human, and the State has not proved anything more than a few loud minutes."),
        timeline: [(0, "Noon: the ticket."), (0, "12:05 p.m.: the scream.")],
        identified: "Street Camera",
        mood: .indifferent,
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let dogBiteSlap = SmallCases.make(
