        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Bite", "{DL} says the dog bit {D.him}.")],
        role: "Passerby",
        exam: [.direct("What did you see on the street at about 6 p.m. on {DATE}?", "\"A dog bit {D} on the leg. The dog was off its leash. Two minutes later, I saw {DL} slap the dog's owner.\""), .direct("What does the street camera show?", "\"It shows {DL} slapping {V}. It shows the two of them close together and the slap.\""), .direct("What injury did {DL} have?", "\"A scrape on the leg from the dog. A bite report documents it.\""), .direct("Where were you when the bite happened?", "\"I was on the sidewalk waiting at the crosswalk about thirty feet away. I saw a brown dog run from a yard and bite {DL} on the calf.\""), .direct("What did {D} do right after?", "\"{D.He} yelled and grabbed the leg, then stood for a moment. The dog's owner came running and tried to take the dog away.\""), .direct("When did the slap happen?", "\"About two minutes later, after {V} had gotten the dog on a leash. {DL} stepped up and slapped {V} across the cheek, and {V} stepped back.\""), .cross("Was the dog off its leash?", "\"Yes. I saw it. It was running loose. I think that's why the bite happened.\""), .cross("Did {V} apologize?", "\"I don't recall. I heard some words but couldn't make them out. It was loud.\""), .cross("Was {V} hurt by the slap?", "\"Not seriously. {V} was startled. I didn't see a mark.\""), .cross("{V} did say sorry at some point, didn't {V.he}?", "\"I heard something like sorry, but I was far away and cannot swear to the words. {V} looked upset and worried.\""), .cross("{D} was bleeding, wasn't {D.he}?", "\"I saw a scrape on {D.his} leg with a little blood. It did not look deep, but {D.he} was limping.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} slapped an owner.", "A bite."),
        allocution: "\"That dog ran at me and bit my leg, and I was in pain and furious, and the owner wasn't doing anything. I slapped the owner in anger, and it wasn't smart. I never meant to injure anyone. I'm sorry, and I'll pay for any harm I caused.\"",
        truths: ("The dog was off leash.", "{DL} had a scrape."),
        defendant: [.direct("What happened with the dog?", "\"It ran at me and bit my leg. I was in pain and furious. The owner wasn't controlling it.\""), .direct("Why did you slap {V}?", "\"I lost my temper. It wasn't smart. I wanted the owner to understand what happened.\""), .direct("Did you mean to hurt {V}?", "\"No. It was a slap out of anger. I didn't mean to injure anyone.\""), .direct("How did the bite feel?", "\"It stung and broke the skin on my calf. I was walking home and did not see the dog until it hit me.\""), .direct("What did the owner say to you?", "\"{V} said the dog was friendly and that it must have been startled. That did not sit right with me when my leg was bleeding.\""), .direct("What did you do after the slap?", "\"I stood there stunned, then walked home and cleaned the wound. I did not look back.\""), .cross("You slapped {V} two minutes after the bite, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I had a couple of minutes to cool off. I didn't.\""), .cross("The camera shows you slapping {V}, doesn't it?", "\"Yes. I'm not denying it. I regret it.\""), .cross("You could have called animal control, couldn't you?", "\"Yes. I should have, yes. I'd do it differently now.\""), .cross("The dog was off its leash, wasn't it?", "\"Yes, running free. I did not see a leash on it at all.\""), .cross("You had a few minutes to cool down, didn't you?", "\"Yes, but I was still angry and in pain. That is not an excuse, and I know it.\"")],
