        openings: ("At 11 p.m., a street camera caught {D} swinging a bat at a city bus bench until it broke five minutes later. The bench was on a busy route, and replacing it cost $700.", "The defense will point to a foolish dare among friends, a person who accepts fault, and an offer to pay for the bench. {D} hurt no one and knows the dare was no excuse."),
