        allocution: "\"I never called anyone about a bill, and I don't know the person who was called. I found some gift cards and didn't buy them for any scam. It is my number, but I did not make those calls. I'm sorry for the homeowner's loss.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} redeemed the cards.", "The phone is registered to {DL}."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you call {V}?", "\"No. I did not call anyone about a bill. I do not know {V.him}.\""), .direct("What about the gift cards?", "\"I found some cards. I did not buy them for a scam. I do not know how they were used.\""), .direct("Is that your phone number on the call record?", "\"Yes. It is my number. But I did not make those calls.\""), .direct("Where is your phone usually kept?", "\"In my pocket or on the kitchen counter. Sometimes friends borrow it when theirs dies.\""), .direct("How did you come to have the gift cards?", "\"A person I know gave me some cards to hold and I redeemed a few for groceries. I did not look closely at where they came from.\""), .direct("Did you call anyone that day about a bill?", "\"No, I called nobody about a utility. I was at work, and I can show my schedule.\""), .cross("The phone is registered to you, isn't it?", "\"Yes. It is mine, but someone else could have used it.\""), .cross("The cards were redeemed by you, weren't they?", "\"I redeemed some cards I found. I did not know where they came from.\""), .cross("Cards found just happen to match $600 from a scam?", "\"It sounds bad, I know. I did not take them from {V.him}.\""), .cross("The number on the call record is yours, isn't it?", "\"Yes, it is my number, and I will not say otherwise.\""), .cross("You redeemed cards bought for the amount of $600, didn't you?", "\"I redeemed some of them. I did not add up the total and I did not think about the source.\"")],
        openings: ("A caller told a homeowner that a utility bill was overdue and demanded $600 in gift cards within two hours. The call came from a phone registered to {D}, and the cards were later redeemed by {DL}.", "The defense witnesses will explain that {D} never made the calls, that others borrowed the phone, and that {DL} redeemed cards without knowing where they came from."),
        closings: ("A call from {D}'s phone, $600 in gift cards, and the cards redeemed by {DL}. This is a scam that targets people who answer the phone in good faith.", "A phone registered to {D} is not the same as a caller. The State has not shown who made the call, and a redeemed card without knowledge is not a crime."),
        timeline: [(0, "Noon: the call."), (0, "2 p.m.: the cards.")],
        identified: "Call Record",
        mood: .indifferent)

    static let payrollCheckCash = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.payrollCheckCash",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Man Cashes Stolen Payroll Check at a Check-Cashing Store"],
        law: "uttering",
        spec: "Uttered a forged check to {V}, a check-cashing store, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D} cashed a stolen payroll check for $480 on {DATE}. The check was cashed at noon, and the payee reported it the next day. {D.He} showed a real ID at the window.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Check", "Endorsement not matching."), E(.statement, 2, "Payee", "Reported the check stolen the next day.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Found", "{DL} says {D.he} was given it.")],
        role: "Teller",
        exam: [.direct("What did you notice about the check?", "\"The endorsement did not match the name on the check. {D} cashed it at the window at noon for $480.\""), .direct("What ID did {D} show?", "\"A real ID, in {D.his} own name. {D.He} did not use a false one.\""), .direct("What happened afterward?", "\"The payee reported the check stolen the next day. We then realized the endorsement was not the payee's.\""), .direct("What does a teller check on a payroll check?", "\"We look at the payee name, the endorsement, the signature, and the ID. We also verify the account and the amount against the printed numbers.\""), .direct("What did you see on this check?", "\"It was a payroll check for $480 made out to someone else. The back had a signature in a different handwriting than the printed name.\""), .direct("What did the defendant say at the window?", "\"{DL} said a friend had asked {DL} to cash it because the friend had no account. I asked for ID and {DL} handed over a valid license.\""), .cross("{D} used {D.his} own ID, didn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes, a real ID. That is not what I usually see with stolen checks.\""), .cross("Did the defendant say where the check came from?", "\"{DL} said a friend gave it to {D.him}. I did not ask more.\""), .cross("Did the defendant act nervous?", "\"No. {D.He} was calm and polite. {D.He} answered every question.\""), .cross("You approved the check at the time, didn't you?", "\"I did. The amount matched, and the signature was close enough for a busy lunch hour.\""), .cross("{D} gave you accurate contact information, didn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes, the address and phone matched the license. That is how deputies reached {DL} afterward.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} cashed a stolen check.", "A gift."),
        allocution: "\"A friend handed me that check and asked me to cash it, and I did it with my real ID at the window. I trusted my friend, and I only know a first name. I'm sorry I got involved in something that cost the payee money. I'll repay the four hundred eighty dollars.\"",
        truths: ("The payee reported it stolen.", "{DL} showed a real ID."),
        defendant: [.direct("Whose check was it?", "\"A friend's. The friend handed it to me to cash, and I did not know it was stolen.\""), .direct("Why did you use your real ID?", "\"Because I had nothing to hide. I thought it was an ordinary favor.\""), .direct("Who gave you the check?", "\"A friend. I know the friend's first name only, and I trusted that person.\""), .direct("How well do you know the friend?", "\"From the neighborhood, for a couple of years. I have a first name and a phone number that no longer works.\""), .direct("What did your friend say about the check?", "\"That it was a paycheck and the bank was closed for the friend that day. I was told I could keep twenty dollars for the favor.\""), .direct("What did you do with the cash?", "\"I handed $460 to the friend outside the bank and kept the rest. I did not spend it on myself in a big way.\""), .cross("The endorsement did not match, did it?", "\"I did not look closely. The friend signed it, and I assumed it was okay.\""), .cross("You cashed a payroll check for $480 that was not yours, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did. I did not know it was stolen.\""), .cross("Can you bring in the friend?", "\"I cannot reach the friend.\""), .cross("You did not read the name on the front, did you?", "\"I saw a name, but I did not compare it to the friend's. I trusted what I was told.\""), .cross("You took twenty dollars for cashing it, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I should have realized that a payment for a favor was strange.\"")],
        openings: ("{D} cashed a payroll check for $480 at noon, showing a real ID. The endorsement did not match the payee's name, and the payee reported the check stolen the next day.", "Listen for the defense evidence, which will show that {D} cashed the check as a favor to a friend, hid nothing, and used {D.his} own license. {D.He} had no idea it was stolen."),
        closings: ("A stolen payroll check, an endorsement that did not match, and {D} at the teller window cashing it. {D.He} took a fee for the favor, and a favor like that raises a question.", "{D} showed a real ID, hid nothing, and believed a friend's check was good. The State must prove {DL} knew it was stolen, and open conduct points the other way."),
        timeline: [(0, "Noon: cashed."), (1, "The payee reports.")],
        identified: "Check",
        mood: .indifferent,
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let mopedWrongWay = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.mopedWrongWay",
        category: .traffic,
        headlines: ["Teens on Mopeds Ride Wrong Way Down Main Street"],
        law: "recklessDriving",
        spec: "Drove carelessly and heedlessly in willful disregard of the rights and safety of others, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: false,
        summary: "{D} rode a moped the wrong way on Main Street on {DATE}. The turn came at 4 p.m., and a deputy stopped the moped three minutes later. Two cars swerved.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Street Camera", "{D} weaves the wrong way."), E(.document, 2, "Street Signs", "One-way signs posted on Main Street.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Lost", "{DL} says {D.he} was lost.")],
        role: "Deputy",
        exam: [.direct("What did you see on Main Street?", "\"At 4 p.m., {D} rode a moped the wrong way down Main Street. Two cars swerved to avoid it.\""), .direct("What does the street camera show?", "\"It shows {DL} weaving the wrong way and speeding up after cars honked.\""), .direct("What signs are posted?", "\"One-way signs are posted on Main Street. They face the wrong-way traffic and are easy to see.\""), .direct("What is Main Street like at 4 p.m.?", "\"It is a one-way downtown street with angled parking and a lot of foot traffic after school lets out. There are one-way signs at every intersection.\""), .direct("How fast was the moped going?", "\"Faster than the cars next to it, maybe twenty-five. It weaved around a parked truck.\""), .direct("How did the stop go?", "\"I turned on my lights and followed the moped for about three blocks. {D.He} pulled over and put the kickstand down without incident.\""), .cross("Was anyone hit?", "\"No. Two cars swerved, but nobody was struck.\""), .cross("Did {D} stop when you signaled?", "\"Yes. I stopped {DL} three minutes later, and {DL} cooperated.\""), .cross("Was the defendant lost?", "\"{D.He} said so. I do not know whether that is true.\""), .cross("The moped was not very fast, was it?", "\"It was perhaps twenty-five miles an hour, which is the limit. It accelerated when drivers honked.\""), .cross("{D} had a valid license, didn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes, and the moped was registered. Everything except the direction was in order.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} rode recklessly.", "Lost."),
        allocution: "\"I was lost on that moped, trying to find a friend's place, and I turned in without noticing the street was one way. I missed the cars and never meant to cause swerving. I'm sorry for scaring two drivers. I'll pay closer attention to signs.\"",
        truths: ("Signs were posted.", "{DL} sped up."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you ride the wrong way on Main Street?", "\"Yes. I did not mean to. I was lost and I turned in without thinking.\""), .direct("Did you see the one-way signs?", "\"No. I missed them. I was looking for another street.\""), .direct("Where were you headed?", "\"I was lost, trying to find a friend's place. I did not know the street layout.\""), .direct("Where were you trying to go?", "\"To a friend's place on the east side. My phone navigation said to turn onto Main, and I did not realize it meant the other direction.\""), .direct("What did you see when you turned?", "\"A lot of headlights coming at me and horns. I did not understand at first, and then my stomach dropped.\""), .direct("Why did you speed up?", "\"I panicked and wanted to get out of the lane. I should have stopped and walked the moped to the curb.\""), .cross("Signs were posted on that street, weren't they?", "\"I know. I did not see them. I should have looked.\""), .cross("You sped up when cars honked, didn't you?", "\"I did. I panicked and wanted to get out of the way.\""), .cross("Two cars swerved to avoid you, didn't they?", "\"Yes. I am deeply sorry. I am glad no one was hurt.\""), .cross("There were one-way signs at the corner, weren't there?", "\"Yes, and I missed them. I was looking at my phone and the street names.\""), .cross("You could have hurt somebody, couldn't you?", "\"I could have. Two cars had to swerve, and I am grateful they were quick.\"")],
        openings: ("At 4 p.m., {D} rode a moped the wrong way down Main Street, past posted one-way signs, and two cars had to swerve. A deputy stopped {DL} three blocks later.", "The defense case is that {D} was lost, missed the signs while following a phone map, and panicked when horns sounded. {DL} stopped promptly for the deputy and had valid papers."),
        closings: ("One-way signs, a moped going the wrong way, and two cars forced to swerve. The camera shows it, and a map app does not excuse ignoring posted signs.", "A lost rider who missed a sign and panicked. No one was hit, and the State must prove more than a mistake that {D} has acknowledged."),
        timeline: [(0, "4 p.m.: the turn."), (0, "4:03 p.m.: the stop.")],
        identified: "Street Camera",
        mood: .indifferent)

    static let beachRoadRace = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.beachRoadRace",
        category: .traffic,
        headlines: ["Rental Car Drivers Race Down Beach Road"],
        law: "recklessDriving",
        spec: "Drove carelessly and heedlessly in willful disregard of the rights and safety of others, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: false,
        summary: "{D} raced a rental car on a beach road on {DATE} past walkers. The race began at 3 p.m., and the deputy stopped the car five minutes later. The posted limit was 25.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Road Camera", "{D} speeds past a crosswalk."), E(.document, 2, "Speed Limit Sign", "A 25 mph sign on the beach road.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Unfamiliar", "{DL} says {D.he} did not know the limit.")],
        role: "Deputy",
        exam: [.direct("What did you see on the beach road at 3 p.m. on {DATE}?", "\"{D} was racing a rental car past walkers. The posted limit was 25 miles an hour. I stopped the car five minutes later.\""), .direct("What does the road camera show?", "\"It shows {DL} speeding past a crosswalk. It shows the car going much faster than a 25 mph road.\""), .direct("Was there a sign?", "\"Yes. A 25 mph sign on the beach road. It's visible to drivers coming in.\""), .direct("What is the beach road like?", "\"A two-lane road along the shore with a wide shoulder and three marked crosswalks. On summer afternoons it fills with families carrying chairs and coolers.\""), .direct("What did you observe about the car?", "\"A white rental sedan came down the road from the north much faster than traffic, and a second car paced alongside it for a stretch. The two seemed to be racing.\""), .direct("What happened at the crosswalk?", "\"A group of walkers stepped into the crosswalk and had to jump back as the sedan swept through at over fifty by my estimate. A parent grabbed a child by the arm.\""), .cross("{DL} says {D.he} did not know the limit, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"It's a rental car, and {D.he} may not have known the road. But a crosswalk with walkers calls for care.\""), .cross("Was anyone hit?", "\"No. Nobody was struck. But walkers had to move aside, and it was close.\""), .cross("How fast was {DL} going?", "\"Well above 25. I can't give you the exact number from memory. The camera shows it.\""), .cross("You did not clock the speed on radar, did you?", "\"Not at that moment. I paced the car for the last stretch and logged it at forty-five or more before I made the stop.\""), .cross("The second car got away, didn't it?", "\"Yes, it turned off at a side road, and I did not have the plate. I stopped the one I could.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} raced.", "Unfamiliar road."),
        allocution: "\"I was in a rental car on vacation and didn't know the road. I was looking at the scenery and never noticed the twenty-five mile limit, and I never thought of it as a race. I'm sorry to the walkers on that road. I'll slow down.\"",
        truths: ("Signs were posted.", "{DL} sped up at a crosswalk."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why were you driving fast?", "\"I was in a rental car on vacation, and I didn't know the road. I felt like the speed limit was higher.\""), .direct("Did you see the 25 mph sign?", "\"I didn't notice it. I was looking at the scenery. If I'd seen it, I'd have slowed.\""), .direct("Were you racing someone?", "\"Not really. I was just driving fast. I didn't think of it as a race.\""), .direct("What was the purpose of your trip?", "\"A week on the coast with two friends. We picked up the rental that morning and had our first real day to see the beach.\""), .direct("What did you think about the other car?", "\"A driver pulled up beside us and gunned the engine, and I laughed and sped up. It was foolish, and I let it turn into a bit of a game.\""), .direct("What did you do when you saw the lights?", "\"I slowed down at once and pulled to the shoulder. I handed over the rental papers and my license and answered every question.\""), .cross("You passed a crosswalk with walkers, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I know that's dangerous.\""), .cross("The deputy stopped you five minutes into it, didn't the deputy?", "\"Yes. I pulled over right away. I was sorry.\""), .cross("The sign was posted, wasn't it?", "\"Apparently. I didn't see it. I should have been looking.\""), .cross("You saw the crosswalk, didn't you?", "\"I saw the white lines, but I did not slow for them, which I regret. People stepped back and I felt awful.\""), .cross("The speed limit sign is large and posted at the entrance, isn't it?", "\"I have been told so. I was watching the other car and the water, and I did not read it.\"")],
        openings: ("On a beach road with a 25 mph limit, {D} drove a rental car at speed past a crosswalk with walkers and was stopped by a deputy five minutes into a race. Signs were posted, and the road camera recorded the car.", "The defense will point to a visitor in a rental car who did not know the road, never saw the signs, and pulled over at once for the deputy. {D} had no thought of hurting anyone."),
        closings: ("A 25 mph limit, a crosswalk full of walkers, and a car speeding past on camera. A visitor still has to read the road.", "A visitor who did not know the road and stopped for the deputy. The State has not proved a deliberate race, only a driver who made a poor choice on an unfamiliar road."),
        timeline: [(0, "3 p.m.: the start."), (0, "3:05 p.m.: the stop.")],
        identified: "Road Camera",
        mood: .indifferent)

    static let firePitFeud = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.firePitFeud",
        category: .publicOrder,
        headlines: ["Man Refuses to Put Out Fire Pit and Threatens Neighbor"],
        law: "disorderly",
        spec: "Disturbed the peace of {V}, a neighbor, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D} kept a smoky fire pit burning on {DATE} and shouted threats at a neighbor. The smoke started at 8 p.m., and deputies arrived at 8:30 p.m. A burn ban was in place.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Porch Camera", "{D} shouts over the fence."), E(.document, 2, "Burn Ban Notice", "A county burn ban notice for that week.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Legal Fire", "{DL} says the fire was legal.")],
        role: "Neighbor",
        exam: [.direct("What happened next door on {DATE}?", "\"{D} kept a smoky fire pit burning starting at 8 p.m. and shouted threats at me over the fence. Deputies arrived at 8:30.\""), .direct("What does your porch camera show?", "\"It shows {DL} shouting over the fence. It shows {DL} yelling and the smoke coming across the yard toward my house.\""), .direct("Was there a burn ban?", "\"Yes. The county had a burn ban in place that week. I have the notice. No outdoor fires were allowed.\""), .direct("How close is {D}'s fire pit to your yard?", "\"It is about fifteen feet from the fence and directly upwind of my back door. The smoke came in thick and gray and smelled like burning plastic and wet wood.\""), .direct("What did you say to the defendant?", "\"I called over the fence that there was a burn ban and asked {DL} to put it out. {DL} said to mind my own business and shouted something about what would happen if I called anyone.\""), .direct("What happened when deputies arrived?", "\"They spoke to {DL} at the fence and told {DL} about the county ban. {DL} put out the fire with a bucket, and the deputies took my statement.\""), .cross("{DL} says the fire was legal, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"The ban notice says otherwise. I can't say what {D.he} knew about it.\""), .cross("Did {DL} touch you or enter your yard?", "\"No. {D.He} stayed on {D.his} side of the fence. It was shouting and smoke, but no physical contact.\""), .cross("What exactly did {DL} say?", "\"I don't recall every word. It was angry and aimed at me. I took it as a threat.\""), .cross("You did not hear the defendant threaten to hurt you directly, did you?", "\"The words were vague, something like you will regret it. I took it as a threat given the tone, but I cannot repeat it exactly.\""), .cross("The smoke did not damage your property, did it?", "\"No, it only drifted over. We closed the windows and went inside for the evening.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} threatened a neighbor.", "A legal fire."),
        allocution: "\"I was relaxing in my yard with a fire pit and thought it was allowed. When the neighbor complained about the smoke, I got angry and said ugly things. I'd never hurt {V}. I'm sorry for the shouting and for the burn ban I didn't know about.\"",
        truths: ("A burn ban was in place.", "{DL} was warned."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why did you have a fire going?", "\"I was relaxing in the yard with a fire pit. I thought it was allowed. I didn't know about the burn ban.\""), .direct("Why did you shout at {V}?", "\"The neighbor was complaining about the smoke, and I got angry. I said things in the heat of the moment I didn't mean.\""), .direct("Did you mean to threaten {V}?", "\"No. I was frustrated and loud. I'd never hurt {V.him}. I'm sorry for what I said.\""), .direct("What was the fire for?", "\"A small backyard fire pit with a few split logs and some branches. I like to sit by it after work and it was a cool evening.\""), .direct("What did you know about burn rules?", "\"I knew there were rules about big yard burns, but I did not know the county had a ban that week. I do not follow county notices.\""), .direct("What did you say to the neighbor?", "\"I was irritated and said something like quit telling me what to do or you will regret it. I did not mean to hurt anybody, and I wish I had kept quiet.\""), .cross("There was a county burn ban, wasn't there?", "\"I've learned that now. I didn't hear about it. I should have checked.\""), .cross("Deputies arrived at 8:30, didn't they?", "\"Yes. I put out the fire when they told me. I cooperated.\""), .cross("You were told about the ban before the deputies came, weren't you?", "\"The neighbor told me over the fence, and I did not believe it. I should have checked the county website.\""), .cross("You kept the fire going after that, didn't you?", "\"Yes, for another half hour, out of stubbornness. I put it out as soon as the deputies spoke to me.\""), .cross("You shouted at {V} after the first warning, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I was angry and I raised my voice over the fence. I meant to be heard, though I know how the words sounded.\"")],
        openings: ("During a county burn ban, {D} kept a smoky fire pit burning from 8 p.m. and shouted threats at a neighbor over the fence. Deputies arrived at 8:30, and a porch camera caught the shouting.", "The defense will present a fire pit lit in an ordinary backyard by someone unaware of a burn ban, and angry words that came from irritation rather than any plan to harm. {D} put the fire out at once for deputies."),
        closings: ("A burn ban in effect, a fire still burning, and threats shouted over the fence on camera. A warning from a neighbor was ignored for half an hour.", "{D} did not know about the burn ban and lost {D.his} temper over smoke complaints. The State has not proved that loud words over a fence were a real threat."),
        timeline: [(0, "8 p.m.: the smoke."), (0, "8:30 p.m.: deputies.")],
        identified: "Porch Camera",
        mood: .indifferent,
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let treeHouseClimb = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.treeHouseClimb",
        category: .publicOrder,
        headlines: ["Man Climbs Into Neighbor's Tree House"],
        law: "trespass2",
        spec: "Entered and remained on the premises of {V}, a neighbor, after being notified not to, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D} climbed into a neighbor's tree house on {DATE} after a warning. {D.He} climbed into the tree house in the evening, and deputies arrived ten minutes later. {D.He} sold the lot years ago.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Yard Camera", "{D} climbs the ladder."), E(.document, 2, "Warning Letter", "A warning to stay off the property.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Childhood", "{DL} says {D.he} built it years ago.")],
        role: "Neighbor",
        exam: [.direct("What happened in your yard in the evening?", "\"{D} climbed up the ladder into the tree house on my property, after being warned to stay off. Deputies arrived ten minutes later.\""), .direct("How long was {D} in the tree house?", "\"About twenty minutes. {D.He} came down when I called out from the porch.\""), .direct("What warning did the defendant receive?", "\"A warning letter telling {DL} to stay off the property. It is in my file.\""), .direct("How did you come to own the property?", "\"I bought the lot from {DL} several years ago. The tree house was already in the oak when I bought it, and I kept it for my children.\""), .direct("Did the defendant keep coming by after the letter?", "\"Once more, a week later. That's when I called the sheriff's office.\""), .direct("What did you see that evening?", "\"The yard camera caught {DL} climbing the ladder around seven. I called the sheriff's office, and deputies arrived about ten minutes later.\""), .cross("{D} sold you that lot years ago, didn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes. {D.He} sold the lot years ago. I know the history.\""), .cross("Did the defendant build the tree house?", "\"Yes, I believe {D.he} built it. It was there when I bought the lot.\""), .cross("Did the defendant damage anything?", "\"No. {D.He} only climbed up. Nothing was damaged.\""), .cross("{D} was gentle with the tree house, wasn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes, {D.he} ran a hand along the wall and sat on the floor. There was no damage that I could see.\""), .cross("{D} left without argument when the deputies came, didn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes, {DL} climbed down and spoke with them calmly. The conversation was brief.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} entered a tree house.", "A childhood project."),
        allocution: "\"I built that tree house myself for my children years ago, and I wanted to see it once more. I sold the lot, and I know it belongs to someone else now. I'm sorry for climbing in after a warning. I'll stay away from that yard.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} sold the lot years ago.", "{DL} built the house."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you climb into the tree house?", "\"Yes, I did. I built that tree house myself years ago for my children, and I climbed up.\""), .direct("Why did you go up there that evening?", "\"It meant a lot to me. I wanted to see it once more, and I knew it was probably my last chance.\""), .direct("When did you sell the lot to {V}?", "\"Years ago. I sold the lot, and I understand that the tree house went along with it.\""), .direct("What is the history of the tree house?", "\"I built it with my own parents for my kids, board by board, over a summer. We spent years up there reading and playing.\""), .direct("Why did you sell the lot?", "\"A job move forced me to sell fast, and I hated leaving the house behind. I have driven past it many times since.\""), .direct("What were you doing that evening?", "\"I wanted to see it one last time because I was moving away again. I figured an hour at dusk would hurt nobody.\""), .cross("You were warned to stay off the property, weren't you?", "\"Yes. I got the letter. I ignored it, because the tree house was sentimental to me.\""), .cross("The property belongs to {V} now, doesn't it?", "\"Yes. I know that. I should not have gone onto the lot without asking.\""), .cross("You could have asked permission to visit, couldn't you?", "\"Yes. In hindsight, yes. I did not want to bother {V.him} with a strange request.\""), .cross("You got the warning letter, didn't you?", "\"Yes, and I kept it in a drawer. I did not respond, and I climbed up anyway.\""), .cross("You never called to ask for permission, did you?", "\"No. I was afraid I would be told no, and I went without asking.\"")],
        openings: ("{D} climbed into a tree house on a neighbor's property in the evening, after a written warning to stay off. Deputies arrived ten minutes later, and the yard camera shows {DL} on the ladder.", "The defense evidence will establish that {D} built the tree house years ago, sold the lot, and returned only to say goodbye to something {DL} made. {D.He} harmed nothing and left peacefully."),
        closings: ("A written warning, a ladder, and {D} climbing it anyway. The property belongs to {V} now, and a warning means exactly what it says.", "A person who built a tree house and wanted to see it once more. Nothing was damaged, and a sentimental visit is not the kind of trespass the law is aimed at."),
        timeline: [(0, "Evening: the climb."), (0, "Evening+10: deputies.")],
        identified: "Yard Camera",
        mood: .indifferent,
        genders: ["D": .male])

