        spec: "Took merchandise valued at $110 from {V}, a bodega, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D} walked out of a bodega with two beer cases on {DATE}. The cooler was open at 8 p.m., and {D.he} walked out five minutes later with the two cases. No tab had been agreed.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Store Camera", "{D} walks out with cases."), E(.statement, 2, "Owner", "No tab was agreed with {D}.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Pay Later", "{DL} says {D.he} meant to pay Friday.")],
        role: "Owner",
        exam: [.direct("What happened at your bodega at 8 p.m. on {DATE}?", "\"The cooler was open, and {D} stood there. Five minutes later, {D.he} walked out with two beer cases.\""), .direct("What does your store camera show?", "\"It shows {DL} walking out with the cases. It shows {DL} going out the door without stopping at the register.\""), .direct("Had you agreed to any tab with {DL}?", "\"No. I never agreed to a tab. I wouldn't have let anyone carry out two cases without paying.\""), .direct("How does your cooler work?", "\"It is a glass-front walk-in near the back wall, and I keep cases of beer on the floor for customers who buy by the case. The register is at the front.\""), .direct("What did you see {D} do?", "\"{D.He} stood at the cooler for a few minutes, then carried two cases up the aisle and straight out the front door without stopping at the counter.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I was on a ladder in the back stocking and could not get down fast enough. By the time I reached the door, {D.he} was already half a block away.\""), .cross("{DL} says {D.he} meant to pay on Friday, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"We never talked about Friday. No one told me anything.\""), .cross("Do you ever run tabs for regulars?", "\"Occasionally, for people I know well. But I decide it in advance, not after the fact.\""), .cross("Did you stop {DL} at the door?", "\"No. I was at the back. I saw it on the camera afterward.\""), .cross("{D} has been a customer before, hasn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes, on and off for a year, a couple of times a week for snacks. We have never discussed a tab.\""), .cross("{D} came back later, didn't {D.he}?", "\"A few days later, yes. I told {DL} I did not give credit, and the matter was resolved when {DL} paid.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} took beer.", "Pay later."),
        allocution: "\"I meant to pay on Friday when I got paid, and I thought the owner would let me run a tab. I should have asked first. I'm sorry to the owner of that bodega. I'll pay for both cases and apologize in person.\"",
        truths: ("No tab was agreed.", "{DL} ran."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why did you walk out with the beer?", "\"I meant to pay on Friday when I got paid. I thought the owner would let me run a tab, since I shop there a lot.\""), .direct("Did you ask the owner about a tab?", "\"No. I assumed it was okay. I should have asked first.\""), .direct("Did you intend to steal the beer?", "\"No. I intended to pay. I came back on Friday, or I planned to. I know I should have asked.\""), .direct("What was your plan for paying?", "\"I get paid on Fridays, and I was short that night. I planned to pay the owner on Friday afternoon and tell the owner what I had taken.\""), .direct("Why did you not talk to the owner at the counter?", "\"I was embarrassed to ask, and a line had formed at the register. I decided to take the cases and settle up in a couple of days.\""), .direct("What happened on Friday?", "\"I came back with the money and told the owner what I owed. The owner was angry, and I understand why.\""), .cross("You never asked, did you?", "\"No. I didn't. I took the cases and left. It looks like theft, and I see why.\""), .cross("The owner never agreed to a tab, did {V.he}?", "\"No. I know now that was a bad assumption.\""), .cross("You walked out five minutes after opening the cooler, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I didn't spend long. I wasn't hiding anything.\""), .cross("You walked out with two cases without asking, didn't you?", "\"Yes, I did. I assumed a tab, and that was a bad assumption.\""), .cross("The owner never offered you credit, did the owner?", "\"No, never. I treated a friendly relationship as an arrangement, and it was not.\"")],
        openings: ("At 8 p.m. {D} opened the cooler at a bodega and walked out five minutes later with two cases of beer, without paying. No tab had been agreed with the owner.", "The defense evidence includes a regular customer who planned to pay on Friday and who took the cases in plain view. {D} came back with the money and told the owner what happened."),
        closings: ("Two cases of beer carried out the door with no payment and no agreement. {D} knew there was no tab, and a promise to pay later is not a purchase.", "{D} is a regular who meant to pay on Friday and walked out in plain view. The State has not proved an intent to steal from an owner {DL} returned to the following week."),
        timeline: [(0, "8 p.m.: the cooler."), (0, "8:05 p.m.: the exit.")],
        identified: "Store Camera",
        mood: .indifferent,
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let registerTwenties = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.registerTwenties",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Cashier Takes Twenties From Register Over a Month"],
        law: "misdLarceny",
        spec: "Stole property of {V}, a store, valued at $560, on or about {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D} took $20 bills from a register over a month. The shortages began thirty days before the audit. The register tapes show the missing $20 bills on {D.his} shifts.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Register Tapes", "Twenties short on {D}'s shifts."), E(.document, 2, "Drawer Recount", "The drawer was recounted and found short.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Counting", "{DL} says counting errors.")],
        role: "Store manager",
        exam: [.direct("What did you notice about the register?", "\"Over about thirty days, $20 bills went missing from the drawer. The register tapes show shortages.\""), .direct("Whose shifts were short?", "\"Only {D}'s shifts. The shortages follow {D.his} schedule and no one else's.\""), .direct("What did the recount show?", "\"We recounted the drawer and found it short again. The twenties were the missing denomination.\""), .direct("How did you spot the pattern?", "\"The weekly cash reports showed the register coming up short by twenty or forty dollars most days. I compared them against the schedule and the gaps fell on one person's shifts.\""), .direct("Who counted the drawer the second time?", "\"Two of us, with the owner watching. We wrote each count on the sheet and signed it.\""), .direct("How much was missing in all?", "\"Over thirty days the shortages added up to about $460, almost all in missing twenty-dollar bills. We started the audit when that figure reached what we could not explain.\""), .cross("Registers make errors, don't they?", "\"They do. But errors do not usually involve only twenties and only one person's shifts.\""), .cross("Did anyone see {D} take cash?", "\"No. I do not have a witness or a video of that.\""), .cross("Did the defendant count the drawer at shift end?", "\"Yes. {D.He} counted it each night and signed the sheet.\""), .cross("Other employees work at that register, don't they?", "\"Occasionally, but only {DL} had it on those shifts. Another employee covers on Sundays, and those days were exact.\""), .cross("You never saw anyone take cash, did you?", "\"No, I have no video of the drawer and no witness. My case is built on the tapes and the schedule.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} took cash.", "Counting errors."),
        allocution: "\"I never took cash from that drawer, and I never put a bill in my pocket. I did make some change errors on busy shifts, and I'm not perfect at counting under pressure. I counted every night and signed the sheet, with nothing to hide. I'm sorry for the shortage, and I'll help sort it out.\"",
        truths: ("Only {DL}'s shifts were short.", "The drawer was recounted."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you take twenties from the register?", "\"No. I did not take any cash from the drawer, and I never put a bill in my pocket.\""), .direct("Could errors explain the shortages?", "\"Yes. I made some change errors during busy shifts. I am not perfect at the register, and the rush gets hectic.\""), .direct("Did you count the drawer at the end of your shift?", "\"Yes. I counted it every night, and I signed the sheet. I did not hide anything.\""), .direct("How busy are your shifts?", "\"Evenings are the busiest. We have lines of ten people at the register and I am often counting change quickly.\""), .direct("What kinds of mistakes can happen?", "\"Giving back a twenty instead of a ten, or miscounting when a customer hands me a stack of bills. I made a few change errors that I noticed afterward.\""), .direct("What did you do when you noticed?", "\"I told the manager when a drawer looked off and wrote it on the sheet. I signed every count, and I had nothing to hide.\""), .cross("Only your shifts were short, weren't they?", "\"Yes, that is what the tapes show. But I did not take anything, and I cannot explain why.\""), .cross("Why only twenties that went missing?", "\"I do not know. Maybe I gave back change wrong for twenties during busy times, but I am not sure.\""), .cross("You count and sign the drawer each night. Don't you know when it is short?", "\"Sometimes I do. I reported it when I saw it. I did not hide a shortage.\""), .cross("Only twenties are missing, aren't they?", "\"So the tapes say. I cannot explain why it was always twenties.\""), .cross("The manager recounted your drawer after those shifts, didn't they?", "\"Yes, the manager recounted my drawer after my shifts. I know the counts came up short, and I cannot explain it.\"")],
        openings: ("Over thirty days, $20 bills went missing from a store register, and the tapes show the shortages on {D}'s shifts only. A recount of the drawer confirmed the gap.", "The defense will present evidence that register errors happen on busy shifts and that {D} counted and signed the drawer each night. No witness and no video shows {DL} taking a dollar."),
        closings: ("Thirty days, only {D}'s shifts short, and only twenties missing from the drawer. These shortages follow one worker's schedule too closely to be luck.", "No witness and no video, only a busy register and a worker who counted and signed each night. A pattern on paper is not proof that {D} took the money."),
        timeline: [(-30, "Shorts begin."), (0, "The audit.")],
        identified: "Register Tapes",
        mood: .indifferent)

    static let groomerCage = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.groomerCage",
        category: .violent,
        headlines: ["Groomer Leaves Dog in Cage Dryer, Dog Overheats"],
        law: "animalCruelty",
        spec: "Intentionally tortured or deprived an animal of necessary sustenance or care, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: false,
        summary: "{D} left a dog in a cage dryer on {DATE} until it collapsed. The dryer ran from 1 p.m. and the dog collapsed at 2 p.m. The timer was set to its top setting.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Shop Camera", "The dryer runs for an hour."), E(.document, 2, "Veterinary Note", "Heat stress; the dog recovered.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Forgot", "{DL} says {D.he} was called away.")],
        role: "Dog owner",
        exam: [.direct("What happened to your dog at the groomer's on {DATE}?", "\"My dog was put in a cage dryer at 1 p.m. and collapsed at 2. The dryer ran for an hour.\""), .direct("What does the shop camera show?", "\"The dryer running for an hour with my dog inside. The timer was set to its top setting.\""), .direct("What did the veterinarian find?", "\"Heat stress. My dog recovered after treatment, but it was dangerous, and I was frightened.\""), .direct("What kind of dog do you have?", "\"A ten-year-old golden retriever mix named for a local park, weighing about seventy pounds. The dog has a bit of arthritis but is otherwise healthy.\""), .direct("What was the plan for the grooming appointment?", "\"A bath, a trim, and a blow dry, about ninety minutes in total. I dropped the dog off at noon and was told I could pick up at two.\""), .direct("How did you learn what happened?", "\"The shop called me at two to say the dog had collapsed and was being rushed to a vet. I drove straight there and found my dog panting on a table.\""), .cross("{DL} says {D.he} was called away, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"A groomer should never leave a dog in a dryer. That's basic.\""), .cross("Did {DL} come back when the dog collapsed?", "\"Eventually, yes. The camera shows the hour. I can't say how quickly after the collapse.\""), .cross("Did {DL} apologize?", "\"I think so. I was too upset to remember. The main thing was getting my dog to the vet.\""), .cross("You watched the shop camera later, didn't you?", "\"Yes, the groomer sent the link after I asked. It shows the cage dryer running from one o'clock until the collapse.\""), .cross("The dog survived and is fine now, isn't it?", "\"Yes, after two days of fluids and rest. The vet said another fifteen minutes could have been fatal.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} overheated a dog.", "A distraction."),
        allocution: "\"I was called away for something urgent and I meant to be right back. A phone call took longer than I expected, and I lost track of time. When I got back, I ran to get that dog out and called for help. I'd never hurt an animal on purpose, and I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("The timer was set to the top.", "{DL} took a long call."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why was the dog in the dryer for an hour?", "\"I was called away for something urgent. I meant to be right back. The timer was higher than I should have set.\""), .direct("What were you called away for?", "\"A phone call that took longer than I expected. I lost track of time. I feel terrible about it.\""), .direct("What did you do when you realized?", "\"I ran back and got the dog out. I called for help. I'd never hurt an animal on purpose.\""), .direct("What do you do before using a cage dryer?", "\"I set the timer, check the airflow, and never go far from the dryer. It is normally a ten or fifteen minute step.\""), .direct("What call pulled you away?", "\"A call about a family emergency from a relative's hospital. I stepped to the back to talk and the conversation ran long.\""), .direct("What did you do when you came back?", "\"I saw the dog lying down and panting and pulled the cage open. I carried the dog to the sink, poured cool water over the paws, and called the owner.\""), .cross("An hour is a very long time, isn't it?", "\"Yes. Much too long. I should never have left the room.\""), .cross("The dog collapsed, didn't it?", "\"Yes. I was horrified. I'm so sorry.\""), .cross("You set the timer at the top setting, didn't you?", "\"Yes, and I set it by habit when I thought I would be busy. That was a serious mistake.\""), .cross("You were on the call for most of an hour, weren't you?", "\"It felt like minutes, but I know the clock says nearly an hour. I should have asked someone to watch the dryer.\""), .cross("You never checked on the dog while the dryer ran, did you?", "\"No. I was on the phone in the back room. I should have set a shorter time and stayed in the room the whole hour.\"")],
        openings: ("A groomer put a dog in a cage dryer at 1 p.m. with the timer on its top setting, and the dog collapsed an hour later. A veterinarian found heat stress, and the shop camera shows the dryer running the whole hour.", "The defense will present a groomer pulled away by an urgent family call, who ran back as soon as the call ended and rushed the dog for help. {D} never meant to harm the animal."),
        closings: ("An hour in a cage dryer, a timer on its top setting, and a dog that collapsed. A groomer is trusted to watch every animal in the shop.", "{D} was called away and meant to be right back. The State has not proved {DL} intended to hurt the dog, and the dog recovered thanks to quick action."),
        timeline: [(0, "1 p.m.: the dryer."), (0, "2 p.m.: the collapse.")],
        identified: "Shop Camera",
        mood: .indifferent)

    static let drumKitVan = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.drumKitVan",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Drum Kit Taken From Church Van"],
        law: "misdLarceny",
        spec: "Stole property of {V}, a church, valued at $1,400, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D} took a drum kit from an unlocked church van on {DATE}. The van was parked on Sunday and the kit was gone on Monday. The lot camera shows {DL} unloading a kit later.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Lot Camera", "{D} unloads a kit."), E(.document, 2, "Equipment List", "The church's drum kit on its inventory.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Gift", "{DL} says a member gave it.")],
        role: "Worship leader",
        exam: [.direct("What went missing from the church van on {DATE}?", "\"Our drum kit. The van was parked on Sunday and unlocked, and by Monday the kit was gone.\""), .direct("How do you know it was the church's kit?", "\"It's on our inventory list. I have the equipment list showing the church's drum kit.\""), .direct("What did the drum kit consist of?", "\"A five-piece kit with cymbals, a kick pedal, and a hardware case, about $1,400 together. We bought it three years ago for the worship band.\""), .direct("How was the kit stored?", "\"In the church van, which was parked in the lot after Sunday service. We load it in on Sunday evenings and unload it for rehearsal on Wednesday.\""), .direct("What does the lot camera show?", "\"The van is parked Sunday night, and on Monday afternoon the same camera shows {D} carrying drum cases from a car toward a different building. I could see the kit's logo on one.\""), .direct("What did the church do after the drum kit was missed?", "\"We checked the van and the lot, and I called the sheriff's office. Our worship leader gave a list of every piece that had been in the van.\""), .cross("{DL} says a member gave it, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"I know of no member who gave away the church's drums.\""), .cross("Was the van locked?", "\"No. It was unlocked. I know that wasn't wise, but it's a church lot and we trusted people.\""), .cross("Can you say the kit on camera is yours?", "\"I can say it looks like ours. I can't say with certainty from the video.\""), .cross("You never saw anyone take the kit out of the van, did you?", "\"No. All I saw was the empty space on Monday and, later, what the lot camera recorded.\""), .cross("Does your kit have a serial number?", "\"Yes, on the bottom of the snare. We gave it to the deputy so they could compare it.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} took a drum kit.", "A gift."),
        allocution: "\"I'd rather not say who gave me that drum kit, and I know that makes it harder. Someone from the congregation offered it to me after church, and I brought it where I planned to use it. I wasn't hiding it. I'm sorry to the church, and I'll make it right.\"",
        truths: ("No member gave it.", "{DL} pawned it."),
        defendant: [.direct("Who was the member?", "\"I'd rather not say. I know that makes it harder. It was someone who attended the church.\""), .direct("Why were you unloading a kit later?", "\"I brought it to where I was going to use it. I wasn't hiding it. I thought it was mine.\""), .direct("How did you get the drum kit?", "\"Someone from the congregation I know only by sight offered it to me after service, saying the church was getting a new one. I took it that evening.\""), .direct("Why did you not get the person's name?", "\"It was a casual conversation in the parking lot and I did not think I would need it. I have been trying to track the person down.\""), .direct("What did you do with the kit?", "\"I took it straight to a pawn shop across town. I needed the money for rent, and the person had told me the kit was mine to keep.\""), .direct("How much did the pawn shop give you for it?", "\"Two hundred dollars. That was far less than a kit like that is worth, and I should have known it meant something was wrong.\""), .cross("The kit was on the church's inventory, wasn't it?", "\"I didn't know. I thought it was donated. I didn't check.\""), .cross("You can't name the member who gave it, can you?", "\"No. I could, but I won't. I understand how it looks.\""), .cross("The van was unlocked, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. It was easy to take things. I took what I was given.\""), .cross("You never confirmed the gift with the worship leader, did you?", "\"No. I did not think of it, and I should have called the office.\""), .cross("The van sat at the church on Sunday and the kit was gone on Monday, wasn't it?", "\"That is what the church says. I took the kit on Sunday evening, and I believed it was mine because of what I was told.\"")],
        openings: ("A church's drum kit sat in an unlocked van on Sunday and was gone on Monday. The lot camera shows {D} carrying a kit from a car later, and the kit matches the church's inventory.", "Jurors will also see a person who says a congregation member gave away the kit, who carried it openly in front of a camera, and who has tried to find the donor. {D} had no idea it was stolen."),
        closings: ("A drum kit on the church's list, missing from the van, and {D} on camera unloading one. No member of the church gave it away, and the van sat unlocked.", "{D} believed the kit was a gift and handled it openly, in a parking lot with a camera. The State has not proved {DL} knew it was taken."),
        timeline: [(0, "Sunday: the van."), (1, "Monday: gone.")],
        identified: "Lot Camera",
        mood: .indifferent)

    static let spotFight = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.spotFight",
        category: .violent,
        headlines: ["Street Performers Fight Over Busking Spot"],
        law: "simpleAssault",
        spec: "Assaulted {V} by striking {V.him}, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D} struck another performer on {DATE} over a corner. {DL} and {V} were setting up on the same corner at about 4 p.m. The punch came ten minutes later.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Street Camera", "{D} hits {V}."), E(.document, 2, "Medical Note", "A bruise on {V}.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "First", "{DL} says {D.he} was there first.")],
        role: "Passerby",
        exam: [.direct("What did you see on the street corner that afternoon?", "\"{D} and {V} were both setting up on the same corner at about 4 p.m., and about ten minutes later {DL} hit {V}.\""), .direct("What does the street camera show?", "\"It shows {DL} striking {V} with a single punch. Then other people stepped in, and it was over within a few seconds.\""), .direct("What was {V}'s injury?", "\"A bruise. A medical note records it. {V} was shaken but able to stand and walk away on {V.his} own.\""), .direct("What was happening on the corner?", "\"It is a busy downtown corner where buskers set up on weekends. Two performers arrived about the same time at four and started unpacking.\""), .direct("What did you hear between them?", "\"A shouting match over who would play there. {V} said {V.he} had been there first, and {DL} said the opposite, and they stood nose to nose.\""), .direct("What did you see the punch look like?", "\"About ten minutes in, {D.he} swung a closed fist and hit {V} on the cheek. {V} stumbled back and dropped a guitar case.\""), .cross("Who arrived on the corner first, if you know?", "\"I cannot say for sure. {V} was already setting up when I walked past on my way.\""), .cross("Did {V} do anything to provoke {D} that you saw?", "\"I did not see anything. They were arguing about the spot, and the argument got loud.\""), .cross("Did the defendant take the spot after the punch?", "\"I believe {D.he} took the spot afterward. I did not watch what happened after the crowd came.\""), .cross("Both of them had gear on the ground, didn't they?", "\"Yes, an amp and a stool each. It was not clear who had set up first.\""), .cross("You did not see a weapon, did you?", "\"No. It was one punch, and then people stepped between them.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} punched a performer.", "A corner."),
        allocution: "\"We argued over that corner, and I lost my temper and swung. I'd been playing there all week and felt {V} took my spot. That's no excuse. I'll find a different place to play and keep my hands to myself.\"",
        truths: ("{V} was setting up.", "{DL} took the spot."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you hit {V}?", "\"Yes, I did. We argued over the corner, and I lost my temper and swung at {V.him}.\""), .direct("Why did you think the corner was yours?", "\"I arrived first. I had been playing on that corner all week, and I felt it was my spot.\""), .direct("Who arrived on the corner first that day?", "\"I did. I got there before {V}, and I felt {V.he} took my spot when {V.he} started setting up.\""), .direct("What do you play?", "\"Saxophone, mostly jazz standards. I have played that corner for three summers and many regulars know me.\""), .direct("What did {V} say that set you off?", "\"That the corner was not mine and I should find another one. After a day of poor tips, that hit a nerve.\""), .direct("What did you do after you punched {V.him}?", "\"I stepped back, shocked at myself. I stayed to see whether {V.he} was all right and gave my name when a bystander asked.\""), .cross("{V} was setting up when you hit {V.him}, wasn't {V.he}?", "\"Yes. {V} was setting up. I should have talked to {V.him} instead of throwing a punch.\""), .cross("You punched a fellow performer over a corner, didn't you?", "\"I did. It was a bad decision, and I regret it a lot. It was not worth it.\""), .cross("The corner is a public space, isn't it?", "\"Yes. Nobody owns it. I know that now, and I should have known it then.\""), .cross("You swung first, didn't you?", "\"Yes. {V} did not hit me, and I will not claim otherwise.\""), .cross("A better answer was to share the corner, wasn't it?", "\"It was. We could have set up fifteen feet apart, and it would have cost neither of us.\"")],
        openings: ("Two street performers were setting up on the same corner at 4 p.m., and ten minutes later {D} punched {V} in the face. A street camera caught the blow, and {V} was left with a bruise.", "The defense case is that {D} arrived first, argued over the corner, and lost a temper in one moment. {D.He} regrets it and stayed to make sure {V} was all right."),
        closings: ("A corner, a dispute, and a punch caught on a street camera. The bruise on {V} shows what {D} did, and an argument over a public spot never justifies a fist.", "One punch in a heated argument over a spot on a public corner. {D} regrets it, and the injury was a bruise that has already faded."),
        timeline: [(0, "4 p.m.: setup."), (0, "4:10 p.m.: the punch.")],
        identified: "Street Camera",
        mood: .indifferent)

    static let bikeLockCutter = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.bikeLockCutter",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Student Cuts Bike Locks Across Campus"],
        law: "misdLarceny",
        spec: "Stole property of {V}, a student, valued at $450, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D} cut a bike lock on {DATE} and rode off. The lock was cut at 1 p.m. and {D.he} rode off three minutes later. The bike was worth $450.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Campus Camera", "{D} cuts the lock."), E(.document, 2, "Bike Registration", "The bike is registered to {V}.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Own Bike", "{DL} says it was {D.his}.")],
        role: "Campus officer",
        exam: [.direct("What did you see on campus at 1 p.m. on {DATE}?", "\"A person cutting a bike lock and, three minutes later, riding off. The campus camera recorded it.\""), .direct("What does the camera show?", "\"It shows {D} cutting the lock. It shows {DL} working on it and then riding away.\""), .direct("Whose bike was it?", "\"The bike is registered to {V}. It's worth $450. The registration is in evidence.\""), .direct("What do you do as a campus officer?", "\"I patrol the lots and bike racks and review the campus camera feeds. Bike thefts are one of the most common reports we get, especially in the afternoon.\""), .direct("How did the bike get tied to {V}?", "\"The frame has a registration sticker that traces to {V}'s student account. {V} reported it missing about twenty minutes after the camera footage.\""), .direct("What exactly did you watch on the footage?", "\"{DL} walks up to the rack with a pair of bolt cutters, squeezes through a thick cable lock, and wheels the bike away. {DL} then mounts it and rides off down the walkway.\""), .cross("{DL} says it was {D.his} own bike, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"But a person who owns a bike has a key and doesn't cut the lock.\""), .cross("Could the registration be wrong?", "\"It could, but I have no reason to think so. It was in {V}'s name.\""), .cross("Did you stop {DL}?", "\"No. I wasn't there at the moment. I reviewed the camera afterward.\""), .cross("{D} did not look around nervously, did {D.he}?", "\"No, {D.he} was calm and moved in a steady way. That is part of why I could not rule out that it was a genuine mistake.\""), .cross("Bikes of the same model look alike, don't they?", "\"The same model in the same color is common on campus. This one had a custom decal that I would expect an owner to recognize.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} cut a lock.", "His own bike."),
        allocution: "\"I'd lost my key, and I needed to get to class, and that bike looked just like mine. I cut the lock believing I was getting my own bike back. I'd never steal one. I'm sorry for the confusion, and I'll pay for the lock and anything I damaged.\"",
        truths: ("The bike was registered to {V}.", "{DL} had bolt cutters."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why did you cut the lock?", "\"I thought it was my bike. I'd lost the key, and I needed to get to class. I cut it and rode off.\""), .direct("Was it your bike?", "\"I believed so. It looked just like mine. I may have gotten confused about which one.\""), .direct("Did you mean to steal?", "\"No. I'd never steal a bike. I thought I was getting my own back.\""), .direct("What kind of bike do you own?", "\"A blue road bike, about the same model as this one. I locked it at the rack near the library three days before.\""), .direct("Why did you carry bolt cutters?", "\"I lost the key to my lock and borrowed cutters from a friend. I planned to cut my own lock and buy a new one.\""), .direct("What did you do after you rode off?", "\"I rode to class and locked it at a different rack with a new chain. I was stopped by a campus officer that afternoon.\""), .cross("Your own bike would have had your own lock, wouldn't it?", "\"I used a lock I always had. I'd lost the key. I wasn't thinking.\""), .cross("The bike is registered to {V}, isn't it?", "\"I know that now. I didn't check anything. I should have, yes.\""), .cross("You cut the lock in broad daylight, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I wasn't hiding. I thought it was mine.\""), .cross("You did not check the registration sticker, did you?", "\"No. I assumed the bike was mine because of its color and rack position.\""), .cross("You never looked at the decal on the frame, did you?", "\"I did not, and I wish I had. A glance would have told me it was not mine.\"")],
        openings: ("At 1 p.m. on campus, {D} cut a bike lock with bolt cutters and rode off three minutes later. The bike, worth $450, is registered to {V}.", "The defense will point to a person who believed the bike was {D.his} own, who cut the lock in daylight in front of a camera, and who rode off without hurrying. {D} had lost a key and a blue bike looked right."),
        closings: ("A bike lock cut on camera, a bike registered to {V}, and {D} riding away. People who own a bike do not need bolt cutters to take it.", "{D} acted openly in daylight and thought the bike was {D.his} own. The State has not proved {DL} knew it belonged to someone else."),
        timeline: [(0, "1 p.m.: the lock."), (0, "1:03 p.m.: the ride.")],
        identified: "Campus Camera",
        mood: .indifferent)

    static let photoPrints = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.photoPrints",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Photographer Takes Payment and Never Delivers Prints"],
        law: "falsePretenses",
        spec: "Obtained property of {V} by deception, $400, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D} took $400 for family prints on {DATE} and never delivered. The shoot was thirty days before the prints were due, and {D.he} stopped answering a month later. {V} had paid $400 up front.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Invoice", "Paid in full."), E(.document, 2, "Messages", "{V}'s unanswered messages about the prints.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Lost Files", "{DL} says the files were lost.")],
        role: "Customer",
        exam: [.direct("What did you pay {D} for?", "\"$400 for family prints, paid up front. The invoice shows it paid in full.\""), .direct("When was the shoot?", "\"Thirty days before the prints were due. I attended the shoot with my family.\""), .direct("What happened after that?", "\"The prints never came. {D} stopped answering my messages about a month later.\""), .direct("What did the package include?", "\"A one-hour family session at a park with about twenty edited prints and a digital gallery. We paid $400 in full when we booked.\""), .direct("How did the shoot go?", "\"{D.He} arrived on time, shot for about an hour, and told us the prints would be ready in thirty days. Everyone seemed happy.\""), .direct("What did you do when the date passed?", "\"I wrote to {D.him} twice and called once. After the third message, nothing came back, and the page I had used went quiet.\""), .cross("{D} says a drive crashed, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes, that is what {D.he} told me eventually. A drive crash is documented.\""), .cross("Did {D} offer a reshoot or a refund?", "\"I do not recall a clear offer. I asked for the prints or my money.\""), .cross("Did the defendant ever send you a single proof or sample from the shoot?", "\"No. I never saw one picture from the session, not even a preview.\""), .cross("{D} did answer you for a couple of weeks, didn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes, at first. {D.He} said the editing was running behind, and then replies stopped.\""), .cross("You do not know about a drive crash except from what the defendant said, do you?", "\"That is true. I only heard about it later, and I never saw documents myself.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} took payment.", "Lost files."),
        allocution: "\"The drive with the photos crashed, and I couldn't recover them. I was embarrassed and stopped answering, which was wrong. I planned to upload to cloud storage and never got to it. I'm sorry to {V}, who paid four hundred dollars and waited. I'll refund it all.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} stopped answering.", "A drive crash is documented."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you deliver the prints?", "\"No. I lost them. The drive with the photos crashed, and I could not recover them.\""), .direct("Did you answer {V}'s messages?", "\"No. I stopped answering. I was embarrassed that I lost the photos.\""), .direct("How did you store the photos?", "\"On an external hard drive and a laptop. I planned to upload to cloud storage after the editing but had not gotten there yet.\""), .direct("What happened to the drive?", "\"It stopped being recognized, and a repair shop said the platter was damaged. They tried to recover the files and could not.\""), .direct("Why did you stop answering?", "\"I was ashamed that I lost the pictures and did not know how to tell a family. I pushed it off week after week.\""), .direct("What did you tell {V} when you took the $400 deposit?", "\"That the prints would be ready in thirty days. I meant it when I said it, and I put the booking in my calendar.\""), .cross("You took $400 up front and delivered nothing, didn't you?", "\"I did. I feel terrible about it.\""), .cross("Why did you not tell {V} the drive crashed?", "\"I was ashamed. I should have called right away.\""), .cross("Have you refunded the $400?", "\"No. I do not have it now. I want to make it right.\""), .cross("You told {V} the prints would be ready in thirty days, and you never sent a single proof, did you?", "\"No. I never sent a proof. I had only started editing when the drive failed, and it is a lot of money for nothing in return.\""), .cross("You say the photos were on a laptop too. Did you check it?", "\"I did. I had only copied a few of the images over before the drive failed, and I could not rebuild the shoot from those. I wish I had called the first week.\"")],
        openings: ("{V} paid $400 up front for family prints from a photo shoot and never received them. {D} stopped answering messages a month after the shoot, and the prints never came.", "Jurors will hear that a drive crash destroyed the photos, that {D} was ashamed and did not know what to say, and that a repair shop documented the failure. {D.He} had no plan to cheat a family."),
        closings: ("$400 paid in full, no prints delivered, and messages ignored for a month. A photographer who loses the photos still owes the family a call.", "A documented drive crash, an embarrassed photographer, and a family who lost their photos. The State has not proved {D} took the money meaning never to deliver."),
        timeline: [(-30, "The shoot."), (0, "Month later: no prints.")],
        identified: "Invoice",
        mood: .indifferent)

    static let swingChains = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.swingChains",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Teen Cuts Chains on Playground Swings"],
        law: "injuryRealProperty",
        spec: "Willfully and wantonly injured real property of {V}, a town, causing damage of $380, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D} cut swing chains at a playground on {DATE}. {D.He} cut the chains at dusk with a saw, and the work was finished five minutes later. The town replaced the chains.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Park Camera", "{D} cuts a chain."), E(.document, 2, "Replacement Invoice", "$380 for four new swing chains.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Prank", "{DL} says it was a prank.")],
        role: "Parks supervisor",
        exam: [.direct("What did you find at the playground?", "\"The swing chains had been cut. A park camera shows {D} cutting a chain at dusk with a saw, and the work took about five minutes.\""), .direct("What did the town have to do?", "\"We replaced four swing chains. The replacement invoice came to $380, and the swings were closed to children until the new chains were in.\""), .direct("How do you know a saw was used?", "\"The cut ends are clean and the camera shows the saw. Another person filmed it, and the clip reached us afterward.\""), .direct("How many children use this playground in a normal week?", "\"On a nice evening we get twenty or thirty kids, and the after-school program uses it most afternoons. The swings are the most popular piece of equipment.\""), .direct("What does the park camera show?", "\"Two figures arrive at dusk, one holding a hand saw. {DL} climbs onto the frame and cuts the first chain while a friend films.\""), .direct("How long did the repair take?", "\"About a week to order and install four new chains with new seat hardware. The invoice came to $380.\""), .cross("Was anyone hurt by the cut chains?", "\"No. The swings were empty at dusk, and no child was using them. We caught it before the next morning.\""), .cross("Did {D} try to hide what was happening?", "\"Not really. {DL} cut the chains in the open and a friend filmed it, which is how we have the video.\""), .cross("Could the chains have been replaced cheaply?", "\"They cost $380 to replace. That is not cheap for a town, but it is not a huge sum either.\""), .cross("How were the chains cut?", "\"With bolt cutters, I think. The cuts were clean and all at the same height.\""), .cross("The cut ends were clean, weren't they?", "\"Yes, a clean saw cut across each chain link. That fits with the camera and with what was filmed.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} cut swings.", "A prank."),
        allocution: "\"A few of us were joking around at dusk, and I cut those chains as a prank. I didn't think about what it would cost the town or the children who play there. A friend filmed it, and I regret that too. I'm sorry, and I'll help pay to replace the chains.\"",
        truths: ("A saw was used.", "{DL} filmed it."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you cut the swing chains?", "\"Yes. It was meant as a prank. I did not think about the cost to the town.\""), .direct("Why did you do it?", "\"A few of us were joking around at dusk. I thought it would be funny, and I did not think it through.\""), .direct("Who filmed it?", "\"A friend of mine filmed it on a phone. I did not think the video would be shared with anyone.\""), .direct("Whose idea was it?", "\"A friend said it would be funny to take down the swings and film it. I grabbed a saw from the garage at home on the way.\""), .direct("What did you feel while you were cutting?", "\"At first I was laughing, then it started to feel wrong. By the fourth chain I was ready to stop.\""), .direct("What happened with the video?", "\"My friend posted it, and the town saw it the next day. I told my parents that same night.\""), .cross("You brought a saw to a playground, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I know how that sounds. It was in my car, and I took it out to do the prank.\""), .cross("Children play on those swings, don't they?", "\"Yes. I know that now, and I regret that. I did not think about children being hurt.\""), .cross("$380 in damage. Will you pay it?", "\"Yes, I would like to. I am sorry, and I should have known better.\""), .cross("You did not have to bring a saw, did you?", "\"No. I picked it up before we left, and I can see how much planning that took.\""), .cross("You climbed onto the frame to reach the chains, didn't you?", "\"Yes, I climbed up on the crossbar to get at the first chain. I know I could have fallen, and I was not thinking about any of it.\"")],
        openings: ("At dusk, {D} cut the chains off four swings in a town playground with a hand saw while a friend filmed. The camera caught it, and the town paid $380 to replace the chains.", "Jurors will also see a thoughtless teenage prank by a person who has admitted it, regrets it, and has offered to pay. {D} struck when the playground was empty."),
        closings: ("A saw, four swing chains, and a camera showing {D} doing it. Cutting playground equipment puts children at risk, whether anyone was there or not.", "A foolish prank with no children present, a full admission, and an offer to pay. That is a young person's mistake, and {D} has taken responsibility for it."),
        timeline: [(0, "Dusk: the saw."), (0, "Dusk+5: done.")],
        identified: "Park Camera",
        mood: .indifferent)

    static let lockChangeBelongings = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.lockChangeBelongings",
        category: .publicOrder,
        headlines: ["Landlord Changes Locks and Keeps Tenant's Belongings"],
        law: "trespass2",
        spec: "Entered and remained on the premises of {V}, a tenant, without legal authority, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D}, a landlord, changed locks and kept a tenant's belongings on {DATE}. The new lock went on in the morning, and the tenant was locked out by evening. No eviction order existed.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Hall Camera", "{D} changes the lock."), E(.document, 2, "Lease", "The lease in the tenant's name.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Rent", "{DL} says rent was overdue.")],
        role: "Tenant",
        exam: [.direct("What happened with your apartment lock?", "\"In the morning, my landlord, {D}, put a new lock on my door. By evening I was locked out of my home with my belongings inside.\""), .direct("What does the hall camera show?", "\"It shows {DL} changing the lock on my door. It is clear and shows {DL} working at the door.\""), .direct("Was there any court order for this?", "\"No. There was no eviction order. The lease is in my name, and no court ever told me to leave.\""), .direct("What is the history of your tenancy?", "\"I rented a one-bedroom apartment for three years under a written lease in my name. I paid rent by check on the first of each month, until I lost hours at work.\""), .direct("What happened that morning?", "\"I left for work at seven, and when I returned in the evening my key did not work. The hall camera shows {DL} changing the lock at about nine.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I called {D.him} and got a recorded message, then called the sheriff's office. A deputy told me that a landlord needs a court order to lock out a tenant.\""), .cross("You owed {D} rent, didn't you?", "\"Yes, I owed about $900. I was behind and I had told {DL} I would pay.\""), .cross("Did the defendant give you notice before changing the lock?", "\"I do not remember a formal notice. I know {D.he} had talked to me about the rent.\""), .cross("Did you get your belongings back eventually?", "\"Yes, later, after I called the sheriff's office. It took more days than it should have.\""), .cross("When was the rent due?", "\"The first of each month. I was behind for two months, and I'd told {D.him} I would catch up.\""), .cross("{D} never told you the date for the lock change, did {D.he}?", "\"No. I saw a note about late rent on my door a week earlier, but nothing about changing the lock.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} locked out a tenant.", "Overdue rent."),
        allocution: "\"{V} was two months behind on rent, and I was losing money, so I changed the locks to protect my property. I didn't know I needed an eviction order first. I'm sorry for locking {V} out and keeping belongings. I'll return everything today.\"",
        truths: ("No eviction order exists.", "{DL} was owed $900."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you change the lock on {V}'s apartment?", "\"Yes. {V} was behind on rent, and I did it to protect my property.\""), .direct("Did you have a court order?", "\"No. I did not know I needed one. I thought I could secure the unit.\""), .direct("How much rent was owed?", "\"$900. {V} was two months behind, and I was losing money.\""), .direct("Did you offer a payment plan?", "\"Yes. I offered to take half now and the rest over two months, and the tenant never answered.\""), .direct("Why did you change the lock?", "\"I thought it was my right as an owner when the rent was overdue. I did not know I needed a court order.\""), .direct("What did you do with the tenant's belongings?", "\"I left them in the apartment and told the tenant they could have them back when the rent was paid. I did not sell or move anything.\""), .cross("You locked a tenant out of a home without a court order, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I know now that is not allowed. I should have gone to court.\""), .cross("{V}'s belongings stayed in the apartment, didn't they?", "\"Yes. I kept them there. I was going to return them when the rent was paid.\""), .cross("Holding belongings until rent is paid is illegal, isn't it?", "\"I understand that now. I did not know the law at the time.\""), .cross("You did not file for eviction, did you?", "\"No. I wanted to avoid the cost and delay of court.\""), .cross("The tenant was locked out of a home with no place to stay, wasn't the tenant?", "\"I did not think that through. I know now that it was a serious problem for the tenant.\"")],
        openings: ("{D}, a landlord, put a new lock on {V}'s door in the morning, locking {V} out of the home by evening. No eviction order existed, and {V}'s belongings stayed behind.", "By the end of this trial, the proof will show that {V} owed $900 in rent and that {D} did not know the law required a court order. {DL} touched no belongings."),
        closings: ("A new lock, a tenant locked out, belongings held, and no court order. A landlord cannot evict a tenant with a screwdriver, whatever the tenant owes.", "A small landlord losing money who did not know the law. A mistake about legal procedure is not the same as a plan to harm a tenant."),
        timeline: [(0, "Morning: new lock."), (0, "Evening: locked out.")],
        identified: "Hall Camera",
        mood: .indifferent)

    static let plowSmash = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.plowSmash",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Plow Driver Smashes Parked Cars on Purpose"],
        law: "injuryPersonalProperty",
        spec: "Willfully and wantonly injured personal property of {V}, causing damage of $1,400, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D} rammed parked cars with a plow blade on {DATE}. It had snowed that morning, and the hit came at 6:30 a.m. Two parked cars took the blade.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Lot Camera", "{D} backs into cars."), E(.document, 2, "Repair Estimates", "$1,400 in total repairs for the two cars.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Slip", "{DL} says the truck slid.")],
        role: "Car owner",
        exam: [.direct("What happened in the parking lot at 6:30 a.m.?", "\"It had snowed that morning, and a plow came in and rammed my parked car and another one with its blade.\""), .direct("What does the lot camera show?", "\"It shows {D} backing the plow into the parked cars. The blade was lowered twice, and the cars took the hits.\""), .direct("What did it cost to repair?", "\"$1,400 in total for the two cars. The repair estimates are in my file.\""), .direct("What were the conditions that morning?", "\"About six inches of fresh snow overnight and it was still coming down lightly at six-thirty. The lot had been sanded the evening before.\""), .direct("Which cars were hit?", "\"Mine, a gray hatchback, and a neighbor's pickup parked next to it. Both were in marked spaces along the back wall of the lot.\""), .direct("What does the camera show about the plow?", "\"The truck backs up toward the wall with the blade up, then drops the blade and rams the hatchback. It pulls forward, then backs and hits the pickup.\""), .cross("Was the lot sanded that morning?", "\"Yes, the lot had been sanded. I know it was not slippery in the way that ice would be.\""), .cross("Could the plow have slid on the snow?", "\"It is possible it slid. But the blade was lowered twice, which does not look like one slide.\""), .cross("Did {D} stop and report the damage?", "\"I do not recall that. I found the damage later, and my insurance had to be involved.\""), .cross("The blade being down twice means it came into contact twice, doesn't it?", "\"The footage shows it hitting my car and then the pickup. It looks like two separate impacts.\""), .cross("The lot was lit when this happened, wasn't it?", "\"There are two lights, one near the front, and the back wall is dim at that hour.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} rammed cars.", "A slide."),
        allocution: "\"It was snowing hard that morning, and I never meant to hit those cars. The plow slid when I backed up and I couldn't stop it in time. Even with sand there was fresh snow on top. I'm sorry to the owners of the two cars, and I'll pay for the repairs.\"",
        truths: ("The blade was lowered twice.", "The lot was sanded."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you hit the parked cars with the plow?", "\"Yes. It was snowing hard, and I did not intend to hit them.\""), .direct("Did the plow slide on the snow?", "\"Yes. It slid when I backed up, and I could not stop it in time.\""), .direct("Was the lot sanded?", "\"Yes, it was sanded. But there was still fresh snow on top, and it was slick.\""), .direct("What was your work that morning?", "\"I was clearing six lots on my route before the stores opened. It had been snowing hard and I was behind.\""), .direct("How did you try to back up?", "\"I looked in the mirrors and saw nothing, then eased back with the blade raised. The truck slid on a patch of ice under the fresh snow.\""), .direct("What did you do after the first hit?", "\"I stopped, tried to pull forward, and slid again. I did not realize the second hit until I got out to look.\""), .cross("The blade came down twice, didn't it?", "\"I think so. I tried to correct after the first hit and made a second one.\""), .cross("You could have looked behind you before backing up, couldn't you?", "\"I did not see the cars through the snow. It was early and dark.\""), .cross("$1,400 of damage. Will your company pay?", "\"I hope so. I am sorry, and I want it fixed.\""), .cross("You dropped the blade as you went, didn't you?", "\"The blade came down when I tried to correct. I know it looks bad on the footage.\""), .cross("You did not leave a note on the cars, did you?", "\"No. I called my dispatcher at once and gave the address, and I assumed the company would call the owners.\"")],
        openings: ("At 6:30 on a snowy morning, a plow backed into two parked cars in a lot, and the camera shows {D} behind the wheel with the blade lowered twice. The repairs cost $1,400.", "The defense will point to a plow driver working in hard snow who slid on slick ground, reported it to dispatch, and stayed at the scene. {D} never meant to hit anything."),
        closings: ("Two parked cars, a plow blade lowered twice, and $1,400 in damage. The camera shows {D} backing into them, and the lot had been sanded.", "A snowy dark morning, a slick surface, and a plow driver who slid. An accident in a snowstorm is not a crime, and {D} reported it right away."),
        timeline: [(0, "6 a.m.: snow."), (0, "6:30 a.m.: the hit.")],
        identified: "Lot Camera",
        mood: .indifferent)

    static let trashCanBlaze = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.trashCanBlaze",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Teen Sets Trash Can Fire Against Building Wall"],
        law: "injuryRealProperty",
        spec: "Willfully and wantonly injured real property of {V}, causing damage of $1,300, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D} lit a trash can against a building wall on {DATE}. The can was lit at 11 p.m., and the fire took hold ten minutes later. The wall was scorched.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Alley Camera", "{D} lights the can."), E(.document, 2, "Repair Estimate", "$1,300 to repair the scorched wall.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Cold", "{DL} says {D.he} meant to warm up.")],
        role: "Building owner",
        exam: [.direct("What did you find at your building?", "\"A trash can had been lit against the wall at 11 p.m., and the fire took hold about ten minutes later. The wall was scorched.\""), .direct("What does the alley camera show?", "\"It shows {DL} moving the can to the wall and then lighting it.\""), .direct("What did the repair cost?", "\"$1,300 to repair the scorched wall. I have the estimate.\""), .direct("What is the alley behind your building like?", "\"A narrow service alley with a dumpster, two trash cans, and a back door for the restaurant on the ground floor. The wall is old brick with a wooden frame above.\""), .direct("What did you see on the camera?", "\"{D.He} drags a metal can from the dumpster to the brick wall, drops in paper from a nearby bin, and lights it. The flame climbs and licks the wall.\""), .direct("How did the fire end?", "\"A passerby saw smoke and called 911. The fire department put it out within a few minutes and the wall was scorched about six feet up.\""), .cross("Where was the can when {D} lit it?", "\"Near the wall. The camera shows the can was moved right up to it first.\""), .cross("Did the fire spread inside the building?", "\"No. It scorched the wall and stopped. The fire department put it out.\""), .cross("Did the defendant stay to watch the fire?", "\"No. {D.He} left after lighting it. I do not know where {D.he} went.\""), .cross("The fire did not enter the building, did it?", "\"No, the brick held. The firefighters said another fifteen minutes and it could have reached the wood frame.\""), .cross("The night was cold, wasn't it?", "\"Very cold, near freezing. I do not doubt that {D.he} was trying to keep warm.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} lit a fire.", "A warm-up."),
        allocution: "\"I was cold, and I lit that trash can to warm myself, and I moved it near the wall to block the wind. I didn't think about how close it was until the fire spread. I'm sorry for scorching the building.\"",
        truths: ("The can was moved to the wall.", "{DL} left."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you light the trash can?", "\"Yes. I was cold, and I lit it to warm up. I did not mean to burn the building.\""), .direct("Why did you light it against the wall?", "\"I moved the can near the wall to block the wind. I did not think the wall would catch.\""), .direct("Where was the can when you lit it?", "\"Near the wall. I did not think about how close it was until the fire spread.\""), .direct("Where were you staying that night?", "\"I had no place, and I was walking through the alley looking for shelter. The wind was biting and I had no gloves.\""), .direct("Why did you set it near the wall?", "\"It blocked the wind from one side. I did not think about how close the flames were to the building.\""), .direct("What did you do when it got bigger?", "\"The fire jumped up the side of the can, and I panicked and walked away. I did not know what else to do.\""), .cross("You moved the can next to the building, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did. It was a bad idea, and I see that now.\""), .cross("You left while the fire was burning, didn't you?", "\"I did. I panicked and walked away. I should have called for help.\""), .cross("A scorched wall is $1,300. Will you pay for it?", "\"I would like to. I did not mean any harm.\""), .cross("You lit it with paper from another bin, didn't you?", "\"Yes, I pulled paper out of a nearby recycling bin. I used a lighter I carry.\""), .cross("You walked away without calling for help, didn't you?", "\"I did. I regret that, and I am glad someone else called.\"")],
        openings: ("At 11 p.m., {D} moved a trash can against the wall of a building and lit it. The fire took hold ten minutes later and scorched the brick, and the repair estimate is $1,300.", "The defense witnesses will explain that {D} was cold, lit the can for warmth, and never meant to harm the building. The fire did not enter the structure, and {D.he} was frightened when it grew."),
        closings: ("A trash can pushed against a building, lit at night, and a person who walked away. The wall was scorched, and the owner faces a $1,300 repair.", "A cold person lighting a fire for warmth and misjudging the distance to a wall. This was carelessness born of desperation, and {D} has taken responsibility."),
        timeline: [(0, "11 p.m.: the can."), (0, "11:10 p.m.: the fire.")],
        identified: "Alley Camera",
        mood: .indifferent)

