        summary: "{D}, an aide, took $240 from a resident's drawer on {DATE}. {D.He} entered the resident's room at 3 p.m., and the cash was found missing that evening. The cash had been counted the day before.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Hall Camera", "{D} enters the room."), E(.statement, 2, "Resident's Family", "Counted the $240 the day before.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Tidying", "{DL} says {D.he} was tidying.")],
        role: "Resident's daughter",
        exam: [.direct("What was in my parent's room drawer?", "\"$240 in cash. I counted it the day before. I count it often so I can keep track for {V}.\""), .direct("What does the hall camera show?", "\"{D}, an aide, entering the room at 3 p.m. After that, the cash was found missing that evening.\""), .direct("What did you find?", "\"The drawer was open and the cash was gone. I had counted $240 the day before, and I was sure.\""), .direct("Who is the resident?", "\"My parent, who lives in a long-term care facility and has some memory trouble. I keep a small amount of cash in the dresser drawer for the barber and snacks.\""), .direct("How do you know the amount?", "\"I counted two hundred and forty dollars in twenties and tens the day before. I wrote it on a card and left the card in the drawer.\""), .direct("What did you tell the staff after you found the cash gone?", "\"I went to the nurses' station and asked who had been in the room. They gave me the aides' schedule, and I called the sheriff's office that night.\""), .cross("{DL} says {D.he} was tidying, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"Aides do tidy. But they don't need to open the cash drawer.\""), .cross("Did you see {DL} take anything?", "\"No. I saw it on the camera later. I wasn't there at 3 p.m.\""), .cross("Could another person have taken it?", "\"I suppose so. Other staff and visitors come in. I can't rule it out.\""), .cross("Other aides and nurses use that hall, don't they?", "\"Yes, it is a busy hall with staff and visitors all afternoon. I do not know who else went into that room.\""), .cross("The drawer was not locked, was it?", "\"No, it was an ordinary dresser drawer. I should have used the lockbox, and I told staff afterward.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} took cash.", "Tidying."),
        allocution: "\"I was tidying the resident's room, as I do every day, and I changed the linens and straightened the drawer. I never opened any drawer for money, and I'd never steal from someone in my care. I'm sorry for the family's worry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} was alone in the room.", "The cash was counted the day before."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why did you go into the room at 3 p.m.?", "\"To tidy up. It's part of my job. I straightened the room and changed the linens.\""), .direct("Did you take the cash?", "\"No. I did not. I never opened any drawer for money. I'd never steal from a resident.\""), .direct("Did you see any cash?", "\"I didn't look for any. I was just tidying. I don't know what was in the drawer.\""), .direct("What tasks do you do in the rooms?", "\"I change linens, empty trash, and wipe surfaces. I open drawers only to put clean clothes away.\""), .direct("What did you do in that room?", "\"I made the bed, emptied the wastebasket, and straightened the nightstand. I did not open the dresser.\""), .direct("What happened when you were told about the money?", "\"I told the supervisor I had not seen cash. I offered to be searched and I cooperated fully.\""), .cross("You were in the room at 3 p.m., weren't you?", "\"Yes. I was there to clean. That's what the camera shows.\""), .cross("The cash was gone that evening, wasn't it?", "\"That's what I hear. I don't know what happened to it.\""), .cross("Other staff come in the room, don't they?", "\"Yes. It's a busy place. Anyone could have.\""), .cross("You were alone in the room for twelve minutes, weren't you?", "\"Yes, when I work a room I am usually alone. That is true of everyone on my shift.\""), .cross("The cash was in the drawer you passed, wasn't it?", "\"I was not told where it was. I did not look in any drawer.\"")],
        openings: ("{V}'s parent had $240 in a drawer, counted the day before. At 3 p.m. the hall camera shows {D}, an aide, entering the room alone for about twelve minutes, and that evening the cash was gone.", "Jurors will also see an aide doing routine tidying in a busy facility where many people come and go. {D} offered to be searched and has no history of taking anything."),
        closings: ("Cash counted at $240 the day before, an aide in the room at 3 p.m., and the drawer empty that evening. The camera puts {D} in that room alone.", "Many people enter that room. {D} was there to tidy, and no one saw any money taken, so the State's case rests on opportunity alone."),
        timeline: [(0, "3 p.m.: the entry."), (0, "Evening: missing.")],
        identified: "Hall Camera",
        mood: .indifferent)

    static let vapeGrab = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.vapeGrab",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Teen Grabs Vape Pens From Counter and Runs"],
        law: "larcenyMerchant",
        spec: "Took merchandise valued at $210 from {V}, a convenience store, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D} grabbed vape pens off a counter on {DATE} and ran. The grab came at 4 p.m., and {D.he} ran a second later. The six pens were worth $210.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Store Camera", "{D} grabs and runs."), E(.document, 2, "Price Tags", "Six vape pens priced at $210 in total.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Dare", "{DL} says it was a dare.")],
        role: "Clerk",
        exam: [.direct("What happened at your counter at 4 p.m.?", "\"{D} grabbed six vape pens off the counter and ran out of the store a second later.\""), .direct("What were the pens worth?", "\"$210 in total. The price tags show six pens at that amount.\""), .direct("What did the store camera show?", "\"It shows {DL} grabbing the pens and running. The whole thing took about two seconds.\""), .direct("Where was the display rack?", "\"On the counter beside the register, within arm's reach of the clerk. Anyone at the counter could see it.\""), .direct("What did you see {D} do?", "\"{DL} came in with another person, looked at the rack for a moment, and then swept all six pens into a coat pocket. {DL} bolted for the door.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I called after {D.him} and then locked the register and phoned the sheriff. I gave a description and handed over the camera file.\""), .cross("Did the defendant return any of the pens?", "\"Yes. {DL} came back later and returned two of them.\""), .cross("Did a friend encourage the defendant?", "\"I heard that a friend urged it. I did not see that part.\""), .cross("Did the defendant threaten you?", "\"No. {D.He} did not say anything. {D.He} just grabbed and ran.\""), .cross("{D} came back later, didn't {D.he}?", "\"A day or so later, yes. {D.He} returned two pens and said sorry, then left before I could ask more.\""), .cross("The other person stayed outside, didn't they?", "\"I think so. I did not see their face, and I cannot say who said what.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} grabbed pens.", "A dare."),
        allocution: "\"A friend dared me, and I wanted to look tough, so I grabbed those pens and ran. I didn't think about the clerk or what it would cost the shop. I brought two back, but I couldn't return the rest. I'm sorry, and I'll pay for all six.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} returned two.", "A friend urged it."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you grab the vape pens?", "\"Yes. It was a dare from a friend, and I did it without thinking.\""), .direct("Why did you do it?", "\"A friend dared me. I wanted to look tough, and I did not think about the consequences.\""), .direct("Did you return any of the pens?", "\"Yes. I brought two back. I could not bring back the rest.\""), .direct("How did the dare start?", "\"A friend said I would never take the whole display, and I wanted to show I could. I did not think it through for a second.\""), .direct("Who did you give the pens to?", "\"A few friends at school. I don't remember who, and I didn't charge anyone for them.\""), .direct("Why did you go back to the store?", "\"I felt sick about it for a day and could not sleep. I returned the two I had and told the clerk I was sorry.\""), .cross("You grabbed six pens and ran, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I know that is stealing. I regret it.\""), .cross("Where are the other four pens?", "\"I gave them away or lost them. I do not have them.\""), .cross("You are willing to pay for the rest?", "\"Yes. I will pay for them. I am so sorry.\""), .cross("You took all six in one motion, didn't you?", "\"Yes, in one sweep. It was not an accident of any kind.\""), .cross("You cannot return the other four, can you?", "\"Not now. I will pay for them.\"")],
        openings: ("At 4 p.m., {D} grabbed six vape pens worth $210 off a store counter and ran. A store camera shows the grab and the run, and a friend stood nearby as {DL} did it.", "The defense case is that {D} acted on a friend's dare, brought back two pens, and wants to pay for the rest. {DL} did not threaten anyone and has expressed real remorse."),
        closings: ("Six pens grabbed off the counter, a run out the door, and $210 in goods gone. {D} took them in one sweep, and returning two does not make up for four.", "A dare from a friend and a foolish grab by someone who returned part of what was taken. {D} wants to repay the rest and has been honest throughout."),
        timeline: [(0, "4 p.m.: the grab."), (0, "4:01 p.m.: the run.")],
        identified: "Store Camera",
        mood: .indifferent)

    static let foodDriveBox = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.foodDriveBox",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Man Takes Canned Goods From Church Food Drive Bin"],
        law: "misdLarceny",
        spec: "Stole property of {V}, a church, valued at $90, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D} took canned goods from a food drive bin on {DATE}. The bin was filled in the evening and was empty by night. The goods were meant for a distribution day.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Hall Camera", "{D} fills a bag."), E(.document, 2, "Donation Log", "Cans logged into the bin for distribution day.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Need", "{DL} says {D.he} needed food.")],
        role: "Church volunteer",
        exam: [.direct("What was the food drive bin for?", "\"Canned goods for a distribution day at our church. The donation log shows cans logged into the bin for that purpose.\""), .direct("What happened to the bin on {DATE}?", "\"It was filled in the evening and empty by night. The goods were meant for distribution day.\""), .direct("What does the hall camera show?", "\"It shows {D} filling a bag from the bin. It shows {DL} loading cans into the bag.\""), .direct("When was the distribution day?", "\"The Saturday after the drive ended. We pack the boxes at the church hall that morning.\""), .direct("What did the bin hold on the evening of the drive?", "\"About sixty cans, mostly vegetables, soup, and beans, plus a few boxes of pasta. I logged them myself and set a sign on the bin.\""), .direct("How did you find out?", "\"I came back to the hall around nine at night and the bin was empty. The hall camera shows {DL} filling a large bag from it a little earlier.\""), .cross("{DL} says {D.he} needed food, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"I have sympathy. We run a food program. {D.He} could have asked.\""), .cross("Did you stop {DL}?", "\"No. I saw it on the camera afterward. I wasn't in the hall at the time.\""), .cross("Did {DL} take everything?", "\"Most of it. The bin was empty by night. I can't say it was all {DL}.\""), .cross("The sign on the bin said donations for distribution day, didn't it?", "\"Yes, in large letters, though in a dim hall it could be missed.\""), .cross("The church also runs a pantry, doesn't it?", "\"Yes, every Thursday evening. Anyone can come in without a question.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} took food.", "Need."),
        allocution: "\"I was hungry and had no money, and I saw that bin and took some cans. I thought it was a collection anyone could take from. I was ashamed and should have asked. I'm sorry to the people who gave and to the families waiting for distribution day.\"",
        truths: ("The bin was for distribution day.", "{DL} could have asked."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why did you take the cans?", "\"I needed food. I was hungry and had no money. I saw the bin and I took what I needed.\""), .direct("Did you know they were for distribution day?", "\"I didn't know. I thought it was a collection anyone could take from. I didn't read the sign.\""), .direct("Why didn't you ask for help?", "\"I was ashamed. I didn't want people to know. I should have asked.\""), .direct("What was your situation that week?", "\"I had lost my job, and my last check had gone to rent. I had not eaten a full meal in two days.\""), .direct("What did you see when you walked into the hall?", "\"A bin of cans with nobody around. I took one can to look at and then kept putting more in the bag.\""), .direct("What did you do with the food?", "\"I took it home and shared it with a neighbor who was also short. I ate two cans of soup that night.\""), .cross("You filled a bag from the bin, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I took more than I needed. I know it was for others.\""), .cross("The cans were meant for a distribution day, weren't they?", "\"I understand that now. If I'd known, I'd have waited.\""), .cross("You could have asked the church for food, couldn't you?", "\"Yes. I know. I let pride get in the way.\""), .cross("Did you tell anyone at the pantry how much you took?", "\"No. I walked out with the bag and said thank you, and I knew I was taking more than the sign allowed.\""), .cross("You could have walked in on Thursday and received food, couldn't you?", "\"I could have. I did not know the pantry's hours, and I was too ashamed to ask.\"")],
        openings: ("Canned goods in a church food drive bin were logged for distribution day. By night the bin was empty, and the hall camera shows {D} filling a large bag from it.", "The defense will point to a hungry person with no money, who took food out of need and did not know it was meant for a distribution day. {D} took it in plain view of a camera."),
        closings: ("Cans logged for distribution day, a bin emptied, and a camera showing {D} filling a bag. The food was meant for many families, not one person's pantry.", "{D} was hungry and took food in plain view of a camera. The State has not proved {DL} knew the cans belonged to a drive, and the church's own pantry offers a better answer than a trial."),
        timeline: [(0, "Evening: the bin."), (0, "Night: empty.")],
        identified: "Hall Camera",
        mood: .indifferent,
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let valveStems = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.valveStems",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Man Cuts Valve Stems on a Row of Cars"],
        law: "injuryPersonalProperty",
        spec: "Willfully and wantonly injured personal property of {V}, causing damage of $240, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D} cut valve stems on six cars on {DATE}. The cuts came at about 1 a.m., and the flats were found at 7 a.m. Six cars were hit.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Street Camera", "{D} crouches at each wheel."), E(.document, 2, "Repair Estimate", "$240 for six valve stems.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Prank", "{DL} says it was a prank.")],
        role: "Car owner",
        exam: [.direct("What did you find on your car?", "\"The valve stem on one of my tires had been cut, and the tire was flat. Six cars on the street were hit.\""), .direct("What did the repair cost?", "\"$240 for six valve stems. The estimate is in my file.\""), .direct("How did you discover the problem?", "\"At seven I came out to leave for work and my right rear tire was flat. I knelt down and found the valve stem cut clean off at the base.\""), .direct("How many cars were affected?", "\"Six on my block, all parked at the curb overnight. We compared notes on the sidewalk and all had the same kind of cut.\""), .direct("What does the street camera show?", "\"At about one a.m., {D} walks down the sidewalk carrying a small tool, crouches at each wheel for a few seconds, and moves on.\""), .direct("How did you learn that other cars on the street were hit too?", "\"A neighbor posted about a flat, and then three more people replied. We walked down the block together and counted six cars.\""), .cross("Was anyone hurt by the flat tires?", "\"No. The cars were parked, and no one was driving. It was a nuisance.\""), .cross("Had {D} argued about parking before?", "\"I have heard {DL} was angry about parking.\""), .cross("How many people complained?", "\"Six car owners, including me. We all had flats in the morning.\""), .cross("Were the tires repaired or replaced?", "\"Most were replaced. A few of us had to find another ride to work while the shop was backed up.\""), .cross("All six cars were hit on the same night, weren't they?", "\"Yes, all six within about an hour, according to the camera. We all found the flat tires at seven in the morning.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} cut stems.", "A prank."),
        allocution: "\"I was tired of people parking in my usual spots on our street, and I let it get to me. I cut those valve stems as a prank without thinking about what it would cost six neighbors. I'm sorry for the flats and the morning they lost. I'll pay for the repairs.\"",
        truths: ("Six cars were hit.", "{DL} was angry about parking."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you cut the valve stems?", "\"Yes. It was a prank, and I did not think about what it would cost people.\""), .direct("Why did you do it?", "\"I was annoyed about the parking on our street. I let it get to me, and I did something stupid.\""), .direct("Were you angry about parking?", "\"A little. People parked in my usual spots, and I was tired of it.\""), .direct("What do you use to cut stems?", "\"A pair of small side cutters from my toolbox. I carried them in my pocket that night.\""), .direct("What was going through your mind?", "\"I had been circling for parking for weeks and ended up two blocks away every night. I wanted the cars to move, and I told myself it was just air in a tire.\""), .direct("What did you do the next morning?", "\"I woke up and felt sick about it. I walked the block and put notes under wipers apologizing.\""), .cross("You cut valve stems on six cars, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I know I hurt people's mornings. I am deeply sorry.\""), .cross("This was at 1 a.m. while everyone slept. Was that a prank?", "\"It seemed like one at the time. I know now it was not.\""), .cross("Will you pay for the repairs?", "\"Yes. I will pay every one of them.\""), .cross("You chose six cars on purpose, didn't you?", "\"I picked cars that I thought belonged to people who had taken my spots. I now think I was wrong about some of them.\""), .cross("The damage comes to $240, doesn't it?", "\"Yes, and I will pay the whole amount. I should have paid with an apology instead of a prank.\"")],
        openings: ("At about 1 a.m., a street camera shows {D} crouching at the wheels of six parked cars and cutting each valve stem. Owners woke to six flats, and replacing the stems comes to $240.", "Jurors will hear that {D} was frustrated about parking, acted in a childish prank, and is ready to pay every owner. {D.He} left notes of apology the next morning."),
        closings: ("Six cars, six cut valve stems, and a camera showing {D} at each wheel. The owners woke to flats and missed their mornings.", "A foolish prank over parking with a small repair bill, and a person who is ready to pay. The State has not proved more than a petty act that {D} regrets."),
        timeline: [(0, "1 a.m.: the cuts."), (0, "7 a.m.: the flats.")],
        identified: "Street Camera",
        mood: .indifferent,
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let sidewalkLie = SmallCases.make(
