        summary: "{D} lay on a sidewalk shouting after closing on {DATE}. The bar closed at 1:45 a.m., and the shouting began at 2 a.m. The bar had stopped serving before closing.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Street Camera", "{D} shouts on the pavement."), E(.statement, 2, "Bar Manager", "Told {D} twice to move.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Drunk", "{DL} says {D.he} was drunk.")],
        role: "Bar manager",
        exam: [.direct("What happened outside your bar?", "\"The bar closed at 1:45 a.m. At 2 a.m., {D} lay on the sidewalk shouting, and I told {D.him} twice to move.\""), .direct("What does the street camera show?", "\"It shows {DL} shouting on the pavement. The video shows {DL} lying down and yelling at people passing by.\""), .direct("Had your bar stopped serving {D}?", "\"Yes. We stopped serving before closing. {D.He} had already had enough.\""), .direct("When does your bar stop serving?", "\"Last call is at 1:30 and we close at 1:45. We stopped serving {DL} about thirty minutes before that after seeing {DL} stumble.\""), .direct("What did the defendant do when the bar closed?", "\"{DL} went outside and lay down on the sidewalk in front of the door. A few minutes later {DL} started shouting at people walking by.\""), .direct("What did you say?", "\"I walked out and told {D.him} to move along or get a ride, and I said it again about ten minutes later. {D.He} did not move.\""), .cross("Did the defendant threaten anyone?", "\"No. {DL} was loud but did not threaten anyone. {DL} just would not leave.\""), .cross("Was the defendant blocking the sidewalk?", "\"Partly. People had to walk around.\""), .cross("Did the defendant move when deputies arrived?", "\"Yes. {D.He} got up when deputies spoke to {D.him}.\""), .cross("{D} did not touch anyone, did {D.he}?", "\"No. {DL} stayed on the pavement and shouted. A couple of people stepped over {DL}'s legs.\""), .cross("Neighbors live above the bar, don't they?", "\"There are apartments above and across the street. Two lights came on while {D.he} was shouting.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} disturbed the peace.", "Drunk."),
        allocution: "\"I'd had too much to drink, and I was being loud and lying on that sidewalk. I should have gone home when the bar stopped serving. I felt dizzy and lay down. I'm sorry to the neighbors and to the deputies, and I'll get a ride home next time.\"",
